e of pagan elements to their religious practices, their caste system, and worship of fire. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:60e41f279e61138ffd24dd6300292b88","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"60e41f279e61138ffd24dd6300292b88","outcome":"meets_criterion","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:67994cd85b93c60bbbcaf18e10673ebc:u_c9d6c96512aab738699ac3da","attribution":"reported_speaker","speaker":"AБ","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"neutral","proposition":"Uzbeks and Tajiks discriminate against Lyuli Roma based on their religious practices.","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","explanation":"The interviewee reports that Uzbeks and Tajiks discriminate against Lyuli Roma by questioning their status as 'real' Muslims due to their specific religious practices.","modelPassage":["urn:doxa:passage:8c607919bde64214f79c61165df6e6ce35f2f5fbc70cf704f8e849a87ecf0d39"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:17757f77bc562727779d3aa4e1832386","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"17757f77bc562727779d3aa4e1832386","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:stereotyping_and_intent:2026-03-operational-1:07d629353e1806de5b8b1a9c1b3000a003614c74470cf23c5ebe4839ea602097","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:67994cd85b93c60bbbcaf18e10673ebc:u_c9d6c96512aab738699ac3da","attribution":"reported_speaker","speaker":"AB","speakerStance":"neutral","documentStance":"neutral","proposition":"Lyuli are not considered 'real' Muslims due to their religious practices.","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","modelPassage":["urn:doxa:passage:8c607919bde64214f79c61165df6e6ce35f2f5fbc70cf704f8e849a87ecf0d39"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:4e95dd3df970987d6a1a776d5135f55f","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"4e95dd3df970987d6a1a776d5135f55f","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:targeted_hostility:2026-03-operational-1:72f7ea3551be2ef7fd32d774ee261f75056cf16c773d8b5a2d7a194b6c879a2d","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:67994cd85b93c60bbbcaf18e10673ebc:u_c9d6c96512aab738699ac3da","attribution":"reported_speaker","speaker":"AB","speakerStance":"neutral","documentStance":"neutral","proposition":"Uzbeks and Tajiks discriminate against Lyuli Roma by questioning their Muslim identity.","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","modelPassage":["urn:doxa:passage:8c607919bde64214f79c61165df6e6ce35f2f5fbc70cf704f8e849a87ecf0d39"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:8b5ad5b35ab8f5611ff6431c4a1fea5f","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"8b5ad5b35ab8f5611ff6431c4a1fea5f","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-racism:exclusion:2025-operational-1:58af664b53f3bbc982a55b72222757384bb7ee5f78fe0304068038feb47eafe4","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:67994cd85b93c60bbbcaf18e10673ebc:u_c9d6c96512aab738699ac3da","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"N/A","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"N/A","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","modelPassage":["urn:doxa:passage:8c607919bde64214f79c61165df6e6ce35f2f5fbc70cf704f8e849a87ecf0d39"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:7c0a3545ae3c68b9cd9f8c1a15878583","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"7c0a3545ae3c68b9cd9f8c1a15878583","outcome":"uncertain","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-racism:institutional_pattern:2025-operational-1:ecbb016b6baf762e73d31e3b32c63b7fc6774025c77f32ff9fd824284fb4ac7b","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:67994cd85b93c60bbbcaf18e10673ebc:u_c9d6c96512aab738699ac3da","attribution":"reported_speaker","speaker":"AБ","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"neutral","proposition":"Uzbeks and Tajiks discriminate against Lyuli Roma as 'unreal' Muslims due to their religious practices.","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","explanation":"The text reports an interviewee's claim that Uzbeks and Tajiks discriminate against Lyuli Roma for their religious practices, but a single passage describing social attitudes is insufficient to establish an evidenced institutional pattern.","modelPassage":["urn:doxa:passage:8c607919bde64214f79c61165df6e6ce35f2f5fbc70cf704f8e849a87ecf0d39"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:cb3f22d8891dff3e697b6f3d37e427d4","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"cb3f22d8891dff3e697b6f3d37e427d4","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-racism:racialization:2025-operational-1:22ba2440d280286f7582830210857fa8b3d81eaaa16f9803c2cd8ab087e9a643","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:67994cd85b93c60bbbcaf18e10673ebc:u_c9d6c96512aab738699ac3da","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"N/A","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"N/A","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","modelPassage":["urn:doxa:passage:8c607919bde64214f79c61165df6e6ce35f2f5fbc70cf704f8e849a87ecf0d39"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","@type":["doxa:SourceVersion","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"gv-699775","title":"Priest wins online anti-prize for Russia's ‘sexist of the year’","author":"Maxim Edwards","translator":[],"publishedOn":"2020-03-09","sourceUrl":"https://globalvoices.org/2020/03/09/priest-wins-online-anti-prize-for-russias-sexist-of-the-year/","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/","contentSha256":"7fed61a5806394f6ecdaf4cd4bb0a406d719d9fb2e55eb14d567323bbbc0d30d","textSha256":"53c034b7a65b186a5220c9a34d4c60799b82ad1c7ba20e41367295d600ba33ee","archivedRecordSha256":"4fd6a9c2831caa25af5352ac782b7ab79b7966b0c52ea0a09fde0cb818e12bc6","inStudy":"urn:doxa:study:muslim-coverage-1"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39:u_7e9697d0e4b33c1a745cd5a5","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_7e9697d0e4b33c1a745cd5a5","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39:u_c1321c308cbe571c88fb4262","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_c1321c308cbe571c88fb4262","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39:u_da07d08d90055149e7908152","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_da07d08d90055149e7908152","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:31e7887012a8268edfb7d810edb600ecfad505802de08d3ce074d2f3f1795df0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00001","start":0,"end":26,"exact":"“Women have weaker minds. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:636b9747b8647e7568f843db67a86f9161aae6dc6801b735eb8340adc30855b5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00001","start":26,"end":212,"exact":"Of course, some Marie Curies can be found here and there, but they're a rarity,” declared Dmitry Smirnov, an Archpriest of the Russian Orthodox Church, live on Radio Radonezh last July. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5abc13ee55b75405a41f3f6b5b6acb0292e19743e2e778f3534b70497b249344","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00001","start":212,"end":358,"exact":"Those words have come back to haunt the cleric, who has won an online vote organised by Russian feminists to identify 2019's “Sexist of the Year.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:35ec886ed4213af51777207804d617e482f01c5dc0b2def84e678cc72c300e33","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00002","start":0,"end":90,"exact":"The Sexist of the Year Award is probably the most high profile “anti-prize” on the RuNet. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:afe597b4136fc4603f894ee21801624ca4c8782c09af9974088a09dc8ba42cad","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00002","start":90,"end":553,"exact":"It is the creation of journalist Natalia Bitten and fellow activists from the For Feminism movement, who aim to raise awareness towards the rise of misogynistic hate speech in Russian public life and the “orgy of sexism in the mass media and advertising.” The vote is held every year on the contest's website from February 23 to International Women's Day on March 8; the final list of contestants is compiled by For Feminism and FemUnity, another activist group. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0d434b1f43a82b9b42323ee8d3b0f90d1d393cb5c70936a37e464bc13d1c4cc3","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00002","start":553,"end":700,"exact":"Their contest has achieved some publicity in recent years, and has an eager following on Facebook and the popular Russian social network VKontakte."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:03e68abb7349c5713cd4c91316261acdf242f24aa48445c1de8f2d8d4d10b61a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00003","start":0,"end":86,"exact":"Bitten and her colleagues are spoilt for choice when it comes for worthy contestants. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:31a211f82cd20789fb955dc1da9b4a69a8f7276cccfe7b2f95feae561c948e3e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00003","start":86,"end":281,"exact":"Several high profile Russians have won the prize: in 2014, columnist Yegor Kholmogorov was crowned sexist of the year for his comments advocating punching women who dared utter the word “sexism.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:646efe325eaccf61d980d79f7f12080f8cd72d7c90129cf3f2cbf81bafcdc6b8","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00004","start":0,"end":97,"exact":"This year, 5,995 votes were cast for the “sexist of the year,” of which Smirnov took 48 percent. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:fc78acd7d72e20a9e9d49288fe782e548fb1cbc9acd961eee92a9ff7aa2fee88","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00004","start":97,"end":337,"exact":"In second place with 39% came Sergey Vostretsov, a State Duma deputy nominated for his suggestion that housewives be punished for “parasitism.” In third and final place with 12% came Dmitry Rogozin, head of Russia's space agency Roskosmos. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e45d083b2fc532e38a586851b8132d8754f32e981af4c6250d63e85cc0d3d472","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00004","start":337,"end":412,"exact":"Rogozin believes that spaceships “should have masculine names, not girls’.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:cb1fcf79976d078a848714cf4b9c7da840a30dda14f7ea58457734dbbf6a1417","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00005","start":0,"end":139,"exact":"Sceptics are also catered for; if there is any doubt that the offending statements are profoundly sexist, each entry offers an explanation."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f3fe0fd76d8f2fdd936195ce19898296ed04e6cdb7fbcd71f993f5a4a9f13c06","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00006","start":0,"end":113,"exact":"What sets this initiative apart is that it does not simply focus on outrageous statements by the usual suspects. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:95f335f4827fb66e6338855ba83e19637a7ac4dbcc2daaf1927b880a3e22e83e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00006","start":113,"end":281,"exact":"Bitten stressed in comments to GlobalVoices that the prize is about more than outbursts of a few public figures, but concerns sexism in Russian public life as a whole. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:fef11236f5b5837dbc7ee59093cb71c1d4e84a5f8ff3227bd383f9af888bc654","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00006","start":281,"end":616,"exact":"Admittedly, all three nominees for 2019 are either close to the ruling party or members of the political elite themselves — while Smirnov's words were particularly egregious, it might not be so surprising to hear them from a cleric; the Russian Orthodox Church, after all, is at the vanguard of the state's cultural conservative drive."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:49564ef7cf3bbb644dc1376d05f03ff62e8aa16d6efb917fb9788eed17bf35f2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00007","start":0,"end":74,"exact":"Far from all of the nominees in past years have been particularly famous. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c40996b138b29968cefcc7d27ec8fc2bbd6793b5972abf6a914585cc8f9a5af8","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00007","start":74,"end":105,"exact":"As the award's website puts it:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:dca21985ddc37cae84d8add9045215b2b89a1973d17b89aee9711c7d9e490857","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00008","start":0,"end":844,"exact":"> Среди тревожных тенденций последнего десятилетия мы констатируем усиление языка вражды в отношении женщин в политике, культуре, СМИ и рекламе. Ситуация усугубляется из-за роста коммерческой составляющей в традиционных медиа и электронных СМИ, куда можно отнести социальные сети и мессенджеры. В общественном дискурсе женщины представлены в качестве предмета потребления при продвижении товаров и услуг. В соответствии с патриархатными нормами, женщины воспринимаются как товар, а товары позиционируются так, как если бы они были женщинами. В российских медиа ширится агрессивная антиженская пропаганда, базирующаяся на фундаменталистских религиозных взглядах и т.н. «традициях». На наш взгляд, цель этой пропаганды — вытеснение женщин из экономической жизни и сегрегация в сфере домашнего неоплачиваемого труда и принудительного деторождения."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ae4f598125acb142b634205fc8f1c8df48e31b440b7d584028f07300bcfef255","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00009","start":0,"end":163,"exact":"> Among the worrying tendencies of the last decade, we note an intensification in hateful language in politics, culture, the media, and advertising towards women. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7a0c551d0f44f1b790e56d0f4e39f98be32e5d6212e55c0616b62e439c3625ad","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00009","start":163,"end":310,"exact":"The situation is worsening due to a growing commercialisation of traditional and online media, which also concerns social networks and messengers. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2d88769d57b6f898b34cf24c73344c222f193fb2501c39462bd627632e44ffc0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00009","start":310,"end":394,"exact":"In public discourse, women are presented as a commodity to sell goods and services. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e43897bb776f45432a4f7679341d18bb4816f7d98188085f3a378dc4087f3494","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39","blockId":"gv-699775-b00009","start":394,"end":523,"exact":"In accordance with patriarchal norms, women are treated as goods to be sold, and goods themselves are sold as if they are women. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:fc68cecf3ed8f0bcdb8ad1f14cf76e2b","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"fc68cecf3ed8f0bcdb8ad1f14cf76e2b","outcome":"not_applicable","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:96f457489e551382ea19273005b15d39:u_7e9697d0e4b33c1a745cd5a5","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:31e7887012a8268edfb7d810edb600ecfad505802de08d3ce074d2f3f1795df0","urn:doxa:passage:636b9747b8647e7568f843db67a86f9161aae6dc6801b735eb8340adc30855b5","urn:doxa:passage:5abc13ee55b75405a41f3f6b5b6acb0292e19743e2e778f3534b70497b249344","urn:doxa:passage:35ec886ed4213af51777207804d617e482f01c5dc0b2def84e678cc72c300e33","urn:doxa:passage:afe597b4136fc4603f894ee21801624ca4c8782c09af9974088a09dc8ba42cad","urn:doxa:passage:0d434b1f43a82b9b42323ee8d3b0f90d1d393cb5c70936a37e464bc13d1c4cc3","urn:doxa:passage:03e68abb7349c5713cd4c91316261acdf242f24aa48445c1de8f2d8d4d10b61a","urn:doxa:passage:31a211f82cd20789fb955dc1da9b4a69a8f7276cccfe7b2f95feae561c948e3e","urn:doxa:passage:646efe325eaccf61d980d79f7f12080f8cd72d7c90129cf3f2cbf81bafcdc6b8","urn:doxa:passage:fc78acd7d72e20a9e9d49288fe782e548fb1cbc9acd961eee