","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"gv-704886","title":"A feeling of hopelessness: Interview with a Uyghur refugee in Turkey","author":"Guest Contributor","translator":[],"publishedOn":"2020-04-30","sourceUrl":"https://globalvoices.org/2020/04/30/a-feeling-of-hopelessness-interview-with-a-uyghur-refugee-in-turkey/","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/","contentSha256":"e49734deec3c25cea2ea1d184b6506718076ea9806951c3efe5bbb79b573d8bc","textSha256":"3ef999a1691acd56bb963d5c185e201e6703c9dad611b42ea15b7b0a5c0a2846","archivedRecordSha256":"718cd8f08d085b3ceb1dff03b43aa03fa65a847dbb4ec6d1a1a520a254181438","inStudy":"urn:doxa:study:muslim-coverage-1"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9:u_12f6c82c0b8856291f0de150","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_12f6c82c0b8856291f0de150","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9:u_aee03d572511619e69d44d00","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_aee03d572511619e69d44d00","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:43bbe432e2ea498456eba5bdbd14a56c62a69724de548746c96d6e6a18d83b34","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00001","start":0,"end":65,"exact":"The author's identity has been kept anonymous for safety reasons."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4296fcb21fdfe3a3455cbeec6d0554a7ee49486a835432fad3c2937a6c15ec05","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00002","start":0,"end":157,"exact":"Starting in 2017, the Uyghur community living in China has been submitted to increased targeting and indiscriminate imprisonment by the Chinese authorities. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2e697e5d78d26539da2e8a8c580f90a11c9b4731eaa6b426f70c3d1dc19f9c75","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00002","start":157,"end":343,"exact":"This policy of racial and religious profiling has led young Uyghurs, who are able, to leave China and remain in exile mostly in other Muslim countries such as Egypt, Turkey and Malaysia."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ee3eac777b3360bb5ea446a3cf93a67c404b42dab120561ac5c7291738d19712","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00003","start":0,"end":205,"exact":"The 11 million Uyghurs living in the western province of Xinjiang in China are a Muslim Turkic nation that has been targeted by Beijing more systematically as Chinese leader Xi Jinping took power in 2012. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c61eec239070ba23a04f4f3ef276a7ed1de581c87e76eb11c9493077fb31d71f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00003","start":205,"end":507,"exact":"Widely portrayed as ‘motherland separatists’ or simply ‘terrorists’ in mainstream Chinese discourse – including government statements and media – the Uyghurs have been deprived of their most basic human rights, including freedom of religion, of movement, and also of transmitting their native language."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b83697e63d103fad88e354a22079610a92384b6e452cd22ef338a2df18031167","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00004","start":0,"end":296,"exact":"The persecution of Uyghurs has translated into different forms: imprisonment, often with heavy sentences of over 10 years, and more recently, internment in camps in which, according to various testimonies and sources, over 1 million Uyghurs – as well as other Muslim minorities — are being kept. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f27dfab642afd85fad50cdb8b3e22e2b0600c14e4e880509495d188565efcc00","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00004","start":296,"end":518,"exact":"Given the secrecy of the internment camps, that China insists on presenting as ‘vocational training centers, exact numbers are difficult to attain but hundreds and possibly thousands are believed to have died while there. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9c7d176d42dc32561e82ee520179e93a9f7c7d9ce2b50e49147247ef5b5c9546","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00004","start":518,"end":590,"exact":"More detailed information is available in the Xinjiang Victims Database."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f50b19059861a4c9f2215c28f3589fb0085818fd24dee06efee47bf86d2e2ba1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00005","start":0,"end":129,"exact":"Global Voices interviewed Ershat Abdul’ehed, a 22-year-old native of Hotan, a city located by the Taklamakan desert in Xinjiang. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:445ed4727573a3def0ea081c612afcce04d9de0f7c92c22e9902663e91c3745a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00005","start":129,"end":280,"exact":"Ershat is now stranded in Turkey as a refugee, while his father and older brother are in China, having been sentenced to 18 and 10 years respectively. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1b47ed13e13c2a085ae34d472d7096ad92caf2fadf206ed305ddbc29128830d1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00005","start":280,"end":602,"exact":"Ershat is unable to return to China as he studied in Egypt, a country Beijing has put on a list of 26 countries deemed “sensitive”, which means any Uyghur lucky enough to have been able to travel, do business or study abroad will interrogated upon return to China and often harassed, sometimes imprisoned or sent to camps."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e364547d12eb1c3433d4f5db307cbf53bc3a14a1977b58b114bb9568bfb850ea","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00006","start":0,"end":76,"exact":"The interview was conducted over the phone in Uyghur and edited for brevity."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6c02258ceb305f01e89aa611a145091431da6fd62cfb1f9040cb266220ea93fe","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00007","start":0,"end":58,"exact":"Global Voices (GV): Why did you decide to travel to Egypt?"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7d9ac999a3d23745d8308e430f39cdc9ba452f5bf6b01bd31e5e05a895a7ec79","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00008","start":0,"end":80,"exact":"> Ershat Abdul'ehed (EA): I just wanted to learn more about my religion, Islam. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9f547f1aa5d8c6f3915bb18e86b679db2e3ec7fd5fb0923fd4f76e341d008faf","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00008","start":80,"end":124,"exact":"My plan was to study and then go back home. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4d58bf33fb710c479bbdda3ab8c6eb6068d8d3b73a3aeafb8d41abf3ee494764","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00008","start":124,"end":229,"exact":"When I went to Egypt for studies in 2015, there was absolutely nothing illegal about doing such a thing. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:15f0e6f109c895c50ff96fb49e72cbf9acb979c3f07c749fe5bb3fd3b8e7e127","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00008","start":229,"end":404,"exact":"My father Abdul’ehed Jume, accompanied me to Egypt to get settled, and then returned home to Hotan, in Xinjiang, where he was running a successful business selling car parts. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4239c780170ff26d318aece8f97d0973039f631ee9f0c38489727fea6506b250","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00008","start":404,"end":484,"exact":"My older brother, Abubekir Abdul’ehed, was also working in the family business. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:03f861fa952f2d46768d1c6cbe407ae7c1d8846e73eb33e8e05e4798f87bf68a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00008","start":484,"end":551,"exact":"In February 2016, Abubekir came to Egypt to visit me for two weeks."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e2a9d1ed014b064b4de03c9f1c16f44d471c373db7e2e2e07a3398d0699d4955","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00009","start":0,"end":26,"exact":"GV: What happened to them?"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:81c70873f518e5c3975833d8a1369154b1b256c8e3f001a6681d8587268eee96","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00010","start":0,"end":136,"exact":"> EA: Both got arrested in early 2017, but we never got any information about the reason for that arrest, so I just have my own theory. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c8ff3f1929d24690520fdaaecc3a5bd0bc90340106a1375dcd83a6b2fba61d38","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00010","start":136,"end":232,"exact":"The only reason I can think of, is that my father is punished for sending me to study in Egypt. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:db465bd3371c0a4ef10c214fc186cbedff73a61aa77cb557bfe37a7101d23369","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00010","start":232,"end":288,"exact":"And for my brother – that he went to Egypt to visit me. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:315da0fcb01bfa009396c9a0dd093ba70ad664c3b4fe6cd75613ab8910564c4e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00010","start":288,"end":415,"exact":"Plus, the Chinese authorities have targeted many wealthy and successful Uyghurs in recent years, and my father is one of them. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a340afa6d211cbab750f925f39f7bf87b8e9f5f1f1d249a8d74907f19162ca8d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00010","start":415,"end":513,"exact":"All my family knows is that both are held in a prison in Ürümqi [the capital of Xinjiang region]. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e673684fd438ebd1b3966711d2445eca85aa6d867b295d91f947a68d1f059cbf","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00010","start":513,"end":697,"exact":"We have no news about their health status or about their charges, and I am particularly worried about my brother because just a month before his arrest, he went through kidney surgery."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ef6f8b90a0c99f855150139c8306516dcfb506b7ac57a96c82f9b78f17e87038","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00011","start":0,"end":58,"exact":"GV: How do you keep in touch with your family in Xinjiang?"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1e0a382d17df0c9192d50a9f6f40bd6937ed99134887b79937b6d8b6a6c584ad","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00012","start":0,"end":35,"exact":"> EA: I am completely cut off now. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ced2fed28e274a1aefe30b67c2a6690f1db8bbb7a13b7fe890f5cedc0b33e04c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00012","start":35,"end":262,"exact":"My relatives deleted us from their Wechat accounts [the main social media app in China], and in the current situation I am also worried that they will get some kind of retaliation from the authorities if I try to contact them. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:bb4f7986962acdad655d7b4bc9f6e7417bc482b632f78cd4dfa23cffb83b9fc1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00012","start":262,"end":406,"exact":"In June 2017, I moved with my mother and sister, who had been visiting me, from Egypt to Turkey, This is the only family I am in touch with now."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:3c4f23bc923422664ff918b2005c9366","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"3c4f23bc923422664ff918b2005c9366","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9:u_12f6c82c0b8856291f0de150","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:43bbe432e2ea498456eba5bdbd14a56c62a69724de548746c96d6e6a18d83b34","urn:doxa:passage:4296fcb21fdfe3a3455cbeec6d0554a7ee49486a835432fad3c2937a6c15ec05","urn:doxa:passage:2e697e5d78d26539da2e8a8c580f90a11c9b4731eaa6b426f70c3d1dc19f9c75","urn:doxa:passage:ee3eac777b3360bb5ea446a3cf93a67c404b42dab120561ac5c7291738d19712","urn:doxa:passage:c61eec239070ba23a04f4f3ef276a7ed1de581c87e76eb11c9493077fb31d71f","urn:doxa:passage:b83697e63d103fad88e354a22079610a92384b6e452cd22ef338a2df180311