doxa:passage:018f1c885db4ab3e6fa8d04d2bbff6d9b5836c8b847f879cf449bdbf0e50a8ff","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00013","start":0,"end":49,"exact":"GV: How do you cope with your new life in Turkey?"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:26f389cd89af7ab0e61386240af1924503c60ca8158a72b879da525a83f640af","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00014","start":0,"end":72,"exact":"> EA: Here I am studying sociology, but I find it very hard to perform. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2d7f08dd7f743d8cce4a6e2bdb959076250aa5a936707219f76a7325f1a06cab","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00014","start":72,"end":239,"exact":"Many Uyghur students in Turkey face a similar situation: we are deeply affected by the fact we are being separated from our parents, and are not able to contact them. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:34260623192cc84f33261ad9a08249ddfa0414ae7c31dc4c009914f271f348f4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00014","start":239,"end":269,"exact":"We are living in a nightmare. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:157d2e4e930456652d5285990d7eb6154e3c1d501eee54f19af0825997068710","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00014","start":269,"end":318,"exact":"We are constantly worried and feel hopelessness. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3a0b6d7f159ffcd053c5dd79f2572c3b3528af14e69fef03ccc3964f181eecf5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00014","start":318,"end":390,"exact":"It’s really difficult to focus on our studies in a situation like this. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ba5994fe75225d504f3c74293030d90d5864f26f6d49ad74d02b544211ff0bf1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00014","start":390,"end":476,"exact":"To me, the future looks very dark, and it’s not possible for me to lead a normal life."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8cf3ab3604a11bf9dcfc0f40761dfd7c6e354a79b25ea9adaf88570f9f74684e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00015","start":0,"end":66,"exact":"GV: How did you decide to become an activist for the Uyghur cause?"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b4655a0d1978aa5721be271099492f8787c418d1397d6f5e710248f9d2399143","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00016","start":0,"end":134,"exact":"> EA: Following the initial shock and despair after learning about the arrests of my father and my brother, I didn’t know what to do. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d376f0052ae73157b0deded0de2324dc236631c704a5ea2cd3eaa03ce90d5efa","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00016","start":134,"end":190,"exact":"I just hoped that what really had happened wasn’t true. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:28528dba423a61ce8d7f64d5473af018c1ef186cfe132ef643b25b962545800c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00016","start":190,"end":286,"exact":"After two years passed without any news from them, I wanted to make a video testimony for them. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3dc6a8ee2942675c72cb21fc43f2419db2d1cf684372ef1cafeaf421b58a751c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00016","start":286,"end":312,"exact":"But my mother stopped me. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d8aaca6f8c7f42f2fecda329a5f0471a8e923b73192196d7514e45f86ea99ed6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00016","start":312,"end":375,"exact":"She was afraid that I would make the situation worse for them. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2237bfb2cc6abc661396a542deeef6d7b5bd8bac0238af699b7bbd45f334a7da","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00016","start":375,"end":441,"exact":"But by 2020, we still had no news, so she agreed to let me do it. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3ca7cf403af16dce684ef19e069ef56bb0846d260e87752d8a0216e12b48978e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00016","start":441,"end":474,"exact":"I have since posted some videos. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8ac940d2c9840914b95fa8200675d9808acd1316359f9ed1ab312244140262e7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00016","start":474,"end":545,"exact":"Besides I started drawing caricatures as another way to draw attention."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c83ecc316ba93cd0b88d7c6bb8625ea7a6d1395f0afefa33d8147f7f748a55bc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00017","start":0,"end":74,"exact":"Here is one of Ershat's pleas for the release of his relatives on YouTube:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:853db64d3d1f104270ab84e0076dd726464ac6f4e9d0f7932f93dbb03119f517","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a286cd1a93fade0ed4c9e67899714fc9","blockId":"gv-704886-b00018","start":0,"end":78,"exact":"The Global Voices community takes the security of our members very seriously. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5bc6cb66ae7fce10b082c65de552dde8015b29fa44fbdff2368d9a93c8ec49e3","@type":["doxa:Passage","