9","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:f56244456cffeb263ddebb962b90e8dc7ef06ae2839abf592774c780da5005b8","urn:doxa:passage:1c4d2e64ea2739cbd422f49a5ea923df29d02957f0b540f6bc322c3273297d39","urn:doxa:passage:d35a1ad4d51d02ff7ec96a1cd0f546b44ecaaa8673a6589a59604cb5753d55db","urn:doxa:passage:bb4141c2c4d9de817d88870a135d57c979ca8e0aaf2a516171cfee417b8eed4c","urn:doxa:passage:6c76e2183689753dc4f3d61ca06dbcfc41ccbbcde634c67442a2360d68ddf62e","urn:doxa:passage:80d662a955fcf6f463488d4bbf2e4bcacca2ca99baf99099f0a749168c69514a","urn:doxa:passage:bd93ce68e8102f6ab3345dfb14ced42a3e52d1281e69c0b6db7cf2301f1efdc6","urn:doxa:passage:7c4edc9cb372aba1af295bc618514da912b564fa981d05aae0c7dda46bb142cb","urn:doxa:passage:77d7dad9821efc7d96c1f11b2ab60bf455620fb6b7b3f96dbc12244a047bc366","urn:doxa:passage:ae969019165846d617df240cf440106e158b14a12c18bf870bcc86082abc9685","urn:doxa:passage:586bbe42c4724b8b6349577165801418a9041eda4c7b154db57fd6d1dafdc6be","urn:doxa:passage:817c90671ec82595c2602a34c2200e8cd32aaaadce7cc7c6f0d6391389079a67","urn:doxa:passage:969314b53e911e025234936c3376fc25681b7644f8e2ebf541c0ae18b36e38a8","urn:doxa:passage:06d8241fa42baf811be33cf37c86e85a3c6ef75febacfb2afa6634fc5b09ec0c","urn:doxa:passage:b039cc06a3d4154383c5b7d51d92d037f4af460a0e99e9ce59306ca977972a3f","urn:doxa:passage:5a396a53acd16dde8fcac599a8329080f69e643e03f2079e5b5d59c2e0c74348","urn:doxa:passage:565b0f3f4dfc60675f4e2e7d4bc87095e7ecdd6203d43b8f965e5ea12a1ed419","urn:doxa:passage:5c2002f6bebf402c90147485075bd61350537d93c46c9d2fe4864e5243da987c","urn:doxa:passage:8a398898124813433ef461bf53a5b831ad7271dba97188db5f94a7036c57d69a"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:46b7dc28ac7c53f27b74551510d77ccad5036ddd3e556888ab8fbd1a6c51770b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00001","start":0,"end":240,"exact":"French President Emmanuel Macron´s tweet expressing his condolences to Serbian President Aleksandar Vučić “and all Serbs” upon hearing of the death of Serbian Orthodox Church Patriarch Irinej because of COVID-19, set off an online backlash."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b3190c55b91beaee1b65d7eee45f87d60c63f4be8da705d51fc0782b946eb6aa","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00002","start":0,"end":134,"exact":"> I phoned president Aleksandar Vucic to express condolences after I received the grave news about the departure of Patriarch Irinej. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5c1e5e471ef232efc9d8d9a1ca786f010966c54f4f8700da56d4e395877b27d7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00002","start":134,"end":175,"exact":"France joins all Serbs in their mourning."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e4b55dd6f8d8901e8b1082a4b04ce53a9bbf4e349b42dbf7f7f5cb3eddca637a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00003","start":0,"end":209,"exact":"His critics demanded consistency with Macron's openly stated positions against religious extremism which is known to fuel hatred and if unchecked, leads to violence, as shown by the Yugoslav Wars in the 1990s."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:bcfc3d6191d0d13d9d95d0c262be2b3ec7f5690677e45fffcc838367f358f779","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00004","start":0,"end":395,"exact":"People in the Western Balkans and beyond were perplexed as to how was it possible for someone who claimed to defend secular, enlightened values in Europe to invest France's institutional political capital into association with a figure who, along with the Serbian Orthodox Church, had come to symbolize everything that is backwards, deeply socially conservative and racist about Serbian society."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:688b49942b09b6f06b711b67d42da2453f4c8812f7fd90ed5a0e6868c9e6a92f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00005","start":0,"end":583,"exact":"A large number of Bosniaks, Albanians, Croats and even some Serbs on Twitter also pointed to the fact that Patriarch Irinej was a notorious genocide denier, a supporter of convicted war criminals army general Ratko Mladić and former president of Republika Srpska Radovan Karadžić, and had claimed that the 2017 genocide verdict for the Serb general was “the devil´s work, by the world´s powerful.” Mladić was found to be guilty of—among other things—the crime of genocide, for ordering the execution of over 8,000 Bosniak civilians, mostly men and boys, after the fall of Srebrenica."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e14c1c0fd556bf4e120738ba9f83b0e2186a8f519cefd6ae2e93a92b9b710640","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00006","start":0,"end":181,"exact":"While Patriarch Irinej´s rhetoric was not as bellicose as that of his war-time predecessor Patriarch Pavle, he was a clear supporter of Greater Serbian nationalism and irredentism. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7015db19e56a24bdf528056a2e356809da3fd9c185cc51087733a6eb084303d2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00006","start":181,"end":319,"exact":"It was evident that the Serbian Orthodox Church during his time in power did nothing to distance itself from the Greater Serbia ideology. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d0b431d36890340d926a1ac691bf2f4eadb9b2e508c5f59f26cfff940ca03cf4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00006","start":319,"end":481,"exact":"The Patriarch himself repeated publicly the mantra that “wherever Serbs lived, be it in Serbia, Bosnia, Vojvodina or Montenegro, or other places, that is Serbia.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2d527499c141080c15c2e0235bcf92ad8d98020d64289e24c8452d1ac3ef6acd","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00007","start":0,"end":87,"exact":"The Serbian Orthodox Church has a long history of supporting Greater Serbian ideology. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:398432ebffea603a45502485e67490945d1e157b1f819ba82b424bd60aac36ce","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00007","start":87,"end":192,"exact":"Irinej´s predecessor openly supported the Serb war effort in Bosnia and Herzegovina, Croatia and Kosovo. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7b83e003f9266defc8f87662bdfcd0c28e70b4027b3151f2faaa411e39794b82","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00007","start":192,"end":338,"exact":"As well as giving shelter to, and promoting war criminals like Milan Lukić, one of the most notorious mass murderers during the Bosnian genocide. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:81d8e63280aa6ce9a07d747ef6011a6c03922959ac6cec95a52ca05af26f8668","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00007","start":338,"end":474,"exact":"In 2011, the Serbian Orthodox Church held a book launch in Belgrade´s biggest church, the Cathedral of St Sava to promote Lukić´s book. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7aa78274180eaee1a03ea49e2cbb0d8df60bf582dc0c58dd093264b803ed6dda","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00007","start":474,"end":598,"exact":"In 2012, Lukić was sentenced to life in prison for his role in massacres that had resulted in the deaths of over 100 people."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9e12d0638c138f1a61f97d95c9e07ef4557d63c95cb98797631043a2ca8476bf","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00008","start":0,"end":329,"exact":"In fact, the role of the Serbian Orthodox Church in fanning the flames of nationalism and ethnic hatred was so transparent that in 1995 it sued three French newspapers; Libération, Le Monde and Le Figaro for articles accusing the Orthodox Church of supporting ethnic cleansing, war crimes and genocide in Bosnia and Herzegovina. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:578c93e0a289e0cb390618dcdd00100a0c5b9f0a9ce0c8fa4079fe38df5b5d3b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00008","start":329,"end":375,"exact":"The Church lost its case in the French court. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:79cf3a8f158a549917b814aa09faaec19f442ef510164fc427981636a87b369a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00008","start":375,"end":435,"exact":"Serbian-American historian and religious scholar Michael A. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0637ca15ae46a91520e7292e33b2752fdd1ac9ab1b13a5c93f16a8cd7bf5b2f4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00008","start":435,"end":518,"exact":"Sells wrote in his 1998 book: The Bridge Betrayed: Religion and Genocide in Bosnia:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4b6ee67bbb24ff78ae5f1a58ee69b5be40011b786eac509bbf6860753959ddd6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00009","start":0,"end":396,"exact":"> “The violence in Bosnia was a religious genocide in several senses: the people destroyed were chosen on the basis of their religious identity; those carrying out the killings acted with the blessing and support of Christian church leaders, the violence was grounded in a religious mythology that characterised the targeted people as race traitors and the extermination of them as a sacred act.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c9a85152f69319d80e53e6562f7e5fdd0b7e84361b5591be8e78e463e943812d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50","blockId":"gv-725386-b00010","start":0,"end":82,"exact":"In June 2019, the Patriarch met with Syrian dictator Bashar al-Assad in Damascus. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:ed47395b69b35f2fef52e4792898b230","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"ed47395b69b35f2fef52e4792898b230","outcome":"not_applicable","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:6b0ccb975d051edea38137c0d5ac0c50:u_0e7feb722abced279a19ee52","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:46b7dc28ac7c53f27b74551510d77ccad5036ddd3e556888ab8fbd1a6c51770b","urn:doxa:passage:b3190c55b91beaee1b65d7eee45f87d60c63f4be8da705d51fc0782b946eb6aa","urn:doxa:passage:5c1e5e471ef232efc9d8d9a1ca786f010966c54f4f8700da56d4e395877b27d7","urn:doxa:passage:e4b55dd6f8d8901e8b1082a4b04ce53a9bbf4e349b42dbf7f7f5cb3eddca637a","urn:doxa:passage:bcfc3d6191d0d13d9d95d0c262be2b3ec7f5690677e45fffcc838367f358f779","urn:doxa:passage:688b49942b09b6f06b711b67d42da2453f4c8812f7fd90ed5a0e6868c9e6a92f","urn:doxa:passage:e14c1c0fd556bf4e120738ba9f83b0e2186a8f519cefd6ae2e93a92b9b710640","urn:doxa:passage:7015db19e56a24bdf528056a2e356809da3fd9c185cc51087733a6eb084303d2","urn:doxa:passage:d0b431d36890340d926a1ac691bf2f4eadb9b2e508c5