y"],"recordId":"u_3b7b0c653529fc3f65afa3b4","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a:u_85594938761c7817023a0e54","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_85594938761c7817023a0e54","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:fb3328ee1dd640b7bba9ea2c264bb99cc1dc18622059d5b78936985e0c0420ee","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00016","start":0,"end":573,"exact":"He added in his comments to Raseef22 that the narrative offered in school textbooks is within the context that “the revolution's triggers were the increasing poverty rates under Mubarak, and the collapse of the economy which led to the Egyptian uprising, then the corrective movement following Mohamed Morsi’ reign through the [2013] revolution of June 30, and the people’s will represented in the election of Abdelfateh-Al Sisi, the current president.” This narrative can be noticed in both history and national education textbooks, whether for middle or secondary levels."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6d085aaf210079ae3b6f55b503f101c552c2a553a0c41b10673074ead93e2505","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00017","start":0,"end":12,"exact":"Shakra says:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0fe7704711dc7b05fce9d16b455e534410edef928c3f2e12c28f12b7c7461b18","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00018","start":0,"end":230,"exact":"> حتى نكتب التفاصيل كاملة كان لا بد من الحصول على شهادات عديدة لمن شاركوا في ثورة يناير وهم شباب الميدان، وأن نحصل أيضاً على وثائق من المجلس العسكري، لكن كل ذلك لم يتوفر لنا، فتم اللجوء لرصد الوقائع الرئيسية التي ترسم السياق العام"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:25f473c10a4d3f0289e79e2eded1f4f5d0f161fd301092648c6e6754e4f72220","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00019","start":0,"end":223,"exact":"> In order to write all the details we had to obtain many testimonies from those who participated in the [2011] revolution, who are the youth that stormed the squares, as well as obtain documents from the Military Council. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:339eb5a892be2f80a773755ad2f4cac0f7ad9578b2aea026c83745844745d8b1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00019","start":223,"end":354,"exact":"But these preconditions were not available to us, hence we resorted to mentioning the clear facts which convey the general context."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:22aa24bef444f0f50fe87a0ca73c8e5db51ac5880b2cf29e666baa4c478c0822","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00020","start":0,"end":209,"exact":"He concludes that “mentioning small details on the January [2011] revolt is the best option for now, given the absence of documents that could be relied on and its unavailability to the Ministry of Education. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:19a5533d57e8723f9e6e4d227f1da6a665806d7deb6e9ccfc55b2db65dde6e45","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00020","start":209,"end":279,"exact":"This is what we were taught as university professors and specialists.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7d9c244f219220a49a39650c3561f6131ac6b6f4405f0efbe2353755a4217c4d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00021","start":0,"end":311,"exact":"Echoing a similar view, Professor Assem el-Desouki, a lecturer of history in Egypt's Helwan University and the author of the current history curricula, said that he has taken part in writing Egypt's history syllabus since 1992, and that the few details describing the January Revolution had to be simple notes. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ad39fd9228c1003a6ac15b650fbe6d6d86a771cbe7abc87ecb81684a504145d0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00021","start":311,"end":520,"exact":"Citing another example he said: “when the 1919 revolt was written about, we did not write the events in details, but mentioned the causes and outcomes, which is what we did with the [2011] January revolution.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:abc3bafa37561dea6c9d0d93879a995814993bc0ceaf4d4df5db7148e00e6a38","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00022","start":0,"end":264,"exact":"According to Professor Dessouki's comments to Raseef22, when writing curricula, it is not possible to quote documents that aren’t from the national archive, while media and press contents are considered secondary resources, as the news they offer are not complete."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7a9ae548b95a9bad20fd39582669119fb1cdd5e2f16702097454e97a1ab7f2ca","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00023","start":0,"end":328,"exact":"He added: “This is why it is necessary to cite official news reports, or documents saved in the National Archives when writing the curricula textbooks, and these documents are released to the public only after 30 years of its events occurring, and therefore, all that is written about the 25 Jan revolution is only brief notes.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:32181f3f86f246ad1db1a10eb9d82ef7fa3b59f8de52cce8b82c59209122eedc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00024","start":0,"end":217,"exact":"Additionally, he said that in adherence to how history is written in curricula, details of the current president's period can not be mentioned, since he is still in office, and history must only deal with past events."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:cd20bcfd95aa4d8e5b8379823b5ee77ad12377f9f8f04cc0986dac80c362dce2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00025","start":0,"end":115,"exact":"These opinions, according to head of the freedoms committee at the Press Syndicate Amr Badr, are “academic views”. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d042f5f792f741df3cdfbec1f621ac8ed5ac166d98f17c92837e58b660ec6ed0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00025","start":115,"end":316,"exact":"He tells Raseef22 that those who wrote history textbooks, especially the parts pertaining to 25 January 2011, deny the progress made by the press, which impose an impactful reality and shape decisions."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:49b346ac16978ce3b7d094f2efd5f9bc13a04bd48146170b61f4724029d011d2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00026","start":0,"end":245,"exact":"Badr, who participated in the 2011 uprising, asked: “If content published on media platforms were professional and objective, and backed by a lot of evidence, why can it not be used as sources for writing history in syllabus textbooks?” He adds:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:bf4b6ff78c9b0c80cdc52ec532af6705427d6e314aa796668e10095e6d708207","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00027","start":0,"end":170,"exact":"> “التاريخ في مصر يكتب فقط من وجهة نظر رسمية، وهو أمر بات مرفوضاً خاصة اليوم في عصر مواقع التواصل الاجتماعي. كتابة التاريخ ليست حكراً على أحد، ويجب تعدد وجهات النظر فيه”."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2bc47b5ae447043220a04ae8057b77afce9f7ed25f43de60c84102670bf9b8e7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00028","start":0,"end":132,"exact":"> In Egypt, history is written solely from the official viewpoint, which is rejected nowadays in the era of social media platforms. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f64650fc205fa3d0d468e2d4b1e511785240df37d638b88fbfca0f0e1ff60106","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00028","start":132,"end":210,"exact":"Writing history is not exclusive to anyone, and should include multiple views."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:af679ecd0ebecd1e0e462f3c2ae4565e82a3502205a0e23fe7ab7dbca406ace7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00029","start":0,"end":46,"exact":"We want to know the full detail of our history"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:128130b098cd0d578f6371dfc4af4faa47b1762ddf1e4fd130136439887e47f0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00030","start":0,"end":81,"exact":"Current and former Egyptian students have varying opinions regarding this topic. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:cf89b56a6347b88870aefc60ec54fe7437460c05a49b872eacc478d4d7eaf7e0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00030","start":81,"end":221,"exact":"Some of are very keen about the full details of 2011 being included in the curricula they study, and others do not pay much attention to it."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:6e27911f161d9c68719c13613035f3d2","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"6e27911f161d9c68719c13613035f3d2","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-mu