47128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-racism:racialization:2025-operational-1:22ba2440d280286f7582830210857fa8b3d81eaaa16f9803c2cd8ab087e9a643","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a:u_3b7b0c653529fc3f65afa3b4","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:a8774ece160aa05a30340b3e5aba4529086455e23dcb7f5ca5f37e461b88a6cc","urn:doxa:passage:45a61527bbd8b87876e72d3498610eff861f665437db2bb94d44c1390bfcbcd4","urn:doxa:passage:426260f8abed4420235b40e368328b4a7f84eb0460201855072dc580a37b0631","urn:doxa:passage:9de520fde66241b7be87fd370ce93509df1776fd40b4403c35e3aa8147d238bc","urn:doxa:passage:b2fdd2340a830678467bc8c18fa553c7dfc59c83f75fce32d746661b881c7199","urn:doxa:passage:c51684b49dbcba7051a19c03970e8105d93c523e6044f25287c845252ef1d2ef","urn:doxa:passage:a79770639f85db5a15c537c0a15bfb76666e8859926c7568e1d4178e64a4d71d","urn:doxa:passage:0d50d62838028d804da1ab407efe72707bb877d523fec4538a6f026fe5a0c677","urn:doxa:passage:6b4b47c3999b987de540508a822e54088a1d80f98e44628104f917832d81c488","urn:doxa:passage:0d98408eb9835403ae223877d4d0a6d274cfc693295e0722a154db69b04934d8","urn:doxa:passage:1dc5e12c21cae09f962590320185eb97e2e62361b4fe3a9762aefef1aaf08332","urn:doxa:passage:245bb86e0731c19ef59c4effed6524956dd926e8610a004b15c8463d1d0990be","urn:doxa:passage:6d407cb6ba7630d5976811fd13fa4b618701233acdeedee359429cb872ac4de5","urn:doxa:passage:ad38c6ae3ad878390f1823c113c31b42825e4097220836d386de2663d14ffa14","urn:doxa:passage:1b9edaead4caedb6b5253138f2207870ccbcb1b57965b09386178a4c6b545d10","urn:doxa:passage:c59ceef32562c53fe3e22e995c20aae272883e790342099cea3b333459014208","urn:doxa:passage:538373cdb5ceeb8236fc80c7d848b775dc4b812c1a82ae102712969fb972e9e4","urn:doxa:passage:9bdd961b50441f302d037e5c1b04ec27d92c6e76991139ef37109ac17e0945bd"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:bf7b7ce18212136e0b3f1f527c69ff3c322a917490db4d02bce20825922b424e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00031","start":0,"end":258,"exact":"Mohammed Fouad, a student in the final year of the history department in Cairo University's Faculty of Arts, said that he felt great pride when the January revolution was mentioned in his secondary school history books, and added in his comments to Raseef22:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e9769c4573966b39d6eef0f5d45acbe60d9feb7dcf2b85780cb7b48d1369816c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00032","start":0,"end":171,"exact":"> هذه الثورة عاصرناها وعاصرها أهلنا. وإن لم أذهب للميدان للمشاركة فيها كنتُ مدركاً لما يحدث، لذلك فإن ذكرها في المناهج كان فخراً لنا وسهلاً علينا لأننا مررنا بهذه الأحداث."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9eab0dec90edb94549566d45b8b23b3c0e46782b0c25440bdc4ea378f23a63e4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00033","start":0,"end":60,"exact":"> We observed this revolution and our parents witnessed it. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:889de5bd34de3d0a80d75c49742273a1996b6db3f68199495d721f61f693b95e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00033","start":60,"end":244,"exact":"Although I never took part in its events, I was aware of what was happening, and that is why we felt pride at its mention in our textbooks – because we had lived through these events.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:122fb7393f10bd9325750afa7fcf1bd92ab3cd6bd82ef68295a601610eb7374e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00034","start":0,"end":220,"exact":"Fouad expressed his hope in teaching the complete events of the 2011 revolt as part of the national syllabuses, alongside 2013's uprising which, he said, enabled the people to get rid of the Muslim Brotherhood's regime. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e2819b7f9614c305fffb83cd8a72e0a53650a8953ea9536c7bbe8aa2985f27a6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00034","start":220,"end":308,"exact":"He added that this is the modern history that needs to be taught to current generations."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a4c42dd98cbbbb72f226a65aa267ec071e128c84557d2ea24d24e00e8c4d4768","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00035","start":0,"end":369,"exact":"As for Amr Khalil, a student in the third grade of secondary education, the inclusion of details about the last decade of the country’s history is not of high importance to him, saying that he is indifferent about studying the 2011 revolution in schools’ textbooks, adding that: “If I want to obtain information about it, there are plenty of platforms online for that. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0296e4d2fc3cc3b3c657379699775a96e277761345e9ec3d27f6dbce101dff5d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00035","start":369,"end":429,"exact":"As for school, all I care about is to pass difficult exams.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ab7a3196b54a59768ce1a669101595dbcc00ffba1ea1b18a78b8bc1ae2a11285","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00036","start":0,"end":352,"exact":"Meanwhile, Mutaz Moustafa, who is a student in the third year of secondary school, was too young when the revolution happened, and was aware of what was taking place but not in great detail, and therefore thinks that what the history textbooks offer is insufficient, doesn't paint a full picture, and does not capture the youths’ taking to the streets."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5bbdb99ab7f043b682d4098fa92ba0401d83cf587d35e61212de8b5718be0dc6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00037","start":0,"end":193,"exact":"“Many of our classmates, if they wanted to know more about what transpired during that year, they get the related information from online sources and not the Ministry of Education's textbooks. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8c9989f2f8f17b2171a20dd061f1772f0937a13533582059039ddd11c4d53f2f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a","blockId":"gv-730425-b00037","start":193,"end":434,"exact":"This is why I see it is important to address this milestone event in great detail in our history books, in order for the generations to know its modern history, take pride in it and of the Egyptian people’s ability to change its government.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:99bb6d6a20a1c31c791d3c4983b87d65","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"99bb6d6a20a1c31c791d3c4983b87d65","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:7f5b5b12d89770a1a76d111438059c1a:u_85594938761c7817023a0e54","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:bf7b7ce18212136e0b3f1f527c69ff3c322a917490db4d02bce20825922b424e","urn:doxa:passage:e9769c4573966b39d6eef0f5d45acbe60d9feb7dcf2b85780cb7b48d1369816c","urn:doxa:passage:9eab0dec90edb94549566d45b8b23b3c0e46782b0c25440bdc4ea378f23a63e4","urn:doxa:passage:889de5bd34de3d0a80d75c49742273a1996b6db3f68199495d721f61f693b95e","urn:doxa:pa