a206780d881d51d","blockId":"gv-731325-b00021","start":93,"end":167,"exact":"Blogger Amalini De Sayrah tweeted about one such protest in December 2020."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0207fbd5ae19e87b5b07587b599eae68eb1d177ca4bad9f65dfdf1de724ed2c1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a0cd64f061915a496a206780d881d51d","blockId":"gv-731325-b00022","start":0,"end":144,"exact":"After months of pressure from local and international communities and the U.N., the government reversed the controversial order on February 25. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5d8492cc7c8e764321d41ad30b4997e5e403ed320e3ce64dfcd83f1947e2aae5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a0cd64f061915a496a206780d881d51d","blockId":"gv-731325-b00022","start":144,"end":186,"exact":"Amnesty International said in a statement:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d7805fc2203622963c4d69fe8a11e2ab52beade187ddab3ed88dda5e4d6c5f25","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a0cd64f061915a496a206780d881d51d","blockId":"gv-731325-b00023","start":0,"end":155,"exact":"> “The decision (reversing the burial ban) is a testament to the tireless struggle of families of victims, activists, and members of the Muslim community.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f9f1039622fdc695d4d6eda2f0d465bc626936eedc95b748cf2f780a6460ef52","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:a0cd64f061915a496a206780d881d51d","blockId":"gv-731325-b00024","start":0,"end":111,"exact":"Over 500 people have died from COVID-19 in Sri Lanka so far, around 300 of whom were from minority communities."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:64148c1ed1c348107ac98b14c296cc2e","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"64148c1ed1c348107ac98b14c296cc2e","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcb