sage:91f51f2e56820397a68f96e94ae5c6dae8f91d92f57c3ee748a77d11182ec7a0","urn:doxa:passage:4fff4577df11d55746eada511eedbda2d2041c0765f09ef56a184ebdbfca1dbb","urn:doxa:passage:da353d274afca593444d3230147b277f9ea1234e6207006f68a7247f1d7a9a17","urn:doxa:passage:32458fcbeaf747b57852f07d0930ee7e1764632c1091fed47c102fefa57a817c","urn:doxa:passage:4b88f2b970614a0f285ad7dae40fb40bafb1d92fc897daef38d1637b16aae259"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8b85fdbdb46fb88f16e3ef88d3248f5d3640c68229f8e4cc60b129b95d0fbd5e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00001","start":0,"end":235,"exact":"Resistance can take many forms, and the recent popular uprising in the Occupied Palestinian Territories (OPT) has seen significant developments in the means Palestinians use to reject the injustices upon them by the Israeli occupation."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:76fcad97aa924ea7e67f7137c3b4c3bd29965fa6658b26cc10834c6aca98f15c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00002","start":0,"end":194,"exact":"Since mid-April, and coinciding with Muslims’ holy month of Ramadan, the Palestinian territories witnessed an escalation of violence as Israel imposed restrictions on Palestinians in Jerusalem. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d575fba9e190b0353ef26a9b7e4bcf172ecb968e7a56cb896f073bd23bd966f1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00002","start":194,"end":441,"exact":"These included increased limitations on gatherings and the most recent efforts to take possession of their homes, as well as another wave of Israeli bombardment on the Gaza Strip that lasted 11 days and in which 248 Palestinians lost their lives. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:845b15773e06e43f7c4643dff5e494beda84dcc4da305e4f653506bc75a6b861","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00002","start":441,"end":530,"exact":"In the face of this latest assault, Palestinians are still coming up with ways to resist."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8e0c22473245a28362137ec1647ac032ecc50517c3c55cd3d7eccdbf3b8a8be7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00003","start":0,"end":192,"exact":"Graffiti took centre stage in these events, sparking confrontations on May 24 between Israeli settlers and police on one hand, and Palestinian citizens on the other, as settlers erased murals."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4f20a2fb102202072c57375dc70c0c00b2ebf885c3d736c4b23a955a82cf7be8","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00004","start":0,"end":171,"exact":"On the same day, balloons painted in the four colours of the Palestinian flag were flown over Sheikh Jarrah, the cradle of the most recent wave of Palestinian resistance. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a5303e889567be59870fbd0f5aed89f3b5a2c6774b152865df9c94182331f460","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00004","start":171,"end":318,"exact":"Israeli army officers were deployed to remove the balloons, as Israel prohibits any reference to the Palestinian flag in the occupied territories. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a1df8bf109f51427ec82fc96c9f1a9c574cc3a5b19070d5cccbc7f78bdf678ae","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00004","start":318,"end":456,"exact":"In 2018, some members of the Knesset, Israel's parliament, sought to impose sanctions against those who raise anti-State banners or flags."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:87cb5b6b54ecfbcd4ffd3aa97f6f71cbcfd73a10da14f6ce9d8bc97b6462103c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00005","start":0,"end":33,"exact":"The resistance didn't end there. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4c5b7cdab41e29b551db8b81031d6dd42ed54787440ddc663b745ea15b37b6bb","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00005","start":33,"end":299,"exact":"When Israelis destroyed Samir Mansour Bookshop, the largest bookstore in Gaza, on May 18, Palestinians celebrated the irony that one of the books to survive the destruction was “Returning to Haifa”, a novel written by Palestinian nationalist author Ghassan Kanafani."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8efbc68491afa21b97f325b7964d8dce426508edcf14c3b60c3d6527b05af005","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00006","start":0,"end":68,"exact":"> In the name of God the merciful we start new happiness; happiness!"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7ae1d6b12f077f851740ef37ee83105e216e36ff595e64a1244a3b756a8f1536","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00007","start":0,"end":207,"exact":"> On 5/18/2021, the #Israeli_occupation bombarded #Samir_Mansour_Library in #Gaza Strip, and one of the remnants of the bombing was the novel of #Returning_to_Haifa for the freedom fighter #Ghassan Kanafani…"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1f72ab3e0f88c9616a5ff1786b4f6ae63eef3973bb8804274b05560418f711e2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00008","start":0,"end":191,"exact":"The following day, as a repudiation of the occupation and an expression of their solidarity with Gaza, young people in Sheikh Jarrah symbolically rebuilt the bookstore in their neighbourhood."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:facde1de3b38e1db1b032f6a65d7a31ad972fa3b9b30f920061cfa7d690d197c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00009","start":0,"end":277,"exact":"> The bookstore was demolished in Gaza… it was rebuilt in the Sheikh Jarrah neighborhood of Jerusalem.” Young men open Samir Mansour's bookstore which was bombed by the occupation in Gaza on the eighteenth of this month, in the Sheikh Jarrah neighborhood of occupied Jerusalem."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a2680224afa4e35fda72b9f424cf0500117df80aa6c471bea3c0a4a46d7e00c1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00010","start":0,"end":208,"exact":"On April 30, as the events had begun unfolding, a young Jerusalemite from the Al-Tur neighborhood known as Daboor and the popular Palestinian rapper Shabjdeed released a rap song called “Inn Ann” on YouTube. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7cfb70ef50db34ee02a1e5dfd7a16fff192b09beb237cf7f26b1d8caf789f8cc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00010","start":208,"end":347,"exact":"In the video, Shabjedeed stands in front of a sign reading “Chivalry Shop” chanting about the resilience of Jerusalem's Palestinian youth. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d944c5ac0c42ab6c64a5746e60f7b563f8b4507dbed1268e00cf189cf9f2c722","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00010","start":347,"end":462,"exact":"At the time of writing, the video has been viewed over 13 million times and has trended in various Arab countries. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:03ccfca73a3fa2ac306d3ee9c2a686a35eecb91db34e2ac16103bdb5d0319b04","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00010","start":462,"end":554,"exact":"The song has since become something akin to an anthem for the popular uprising in Palestine."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ffdcd03c8cfeeb9dda5ade3a295b69732095d49e1cd8fac50e43230423653d5f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00011","start":0,"end":17,"exact":"Awni Bilal wrote:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:57578ffcfe97fce8dd85119dba41517e9f8a2fcb62f6f9694e171796222f5303","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00012","start":0,"end":82,"exact":"> Lately, I've been thinking of young and decent Daboor's song, entitled Inn Ann. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0821f95290ec8012a319662072311aa706cd635c4e7b481dadfa1008981f1787","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00012","start":82,"end":213,"exact":"What is the secret behind the glue this work has been covered with, for it to stick in one's imagination and memory in such a way? "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:48809e9263c1afee33044326aed0008be8e8bd57aac253c40a6d0ecb432c26b3","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00012","start":213,"end":386,"exact":"All my traditional barricades and poetic defense lines were pierced by the owner of The Chivalry Shop, Daboor, as he called on the bastards to be bereaved by their mothers. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8abed1f8f26c86872b9498381b953c57dbb64856a1a5dcd117bf687b3b1990cb","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00012","start":386,"end":441,"exact":"Attack me, but there is a poetry pulsation in the text."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f06a6a558f793ec07a790cd1c2bfb253da52f768a688bba4f335a97b28155dfc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00013","start":0,"end":132,"exact":"Employing the local Jerusalem dialect, with some Hebrew words, the song has also become a secret code among the youth of Jerusalem. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c4ad111995ac8f395ccb498a0386c7d6e4643b66720021bbe68f664a6eb7049b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00013","start":132,"end":221,"exact":"Journalist Ali Obaidaat posted on Facebook an account of how its verses played that role:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:599db8927f9c4a253d0510fac61545e3f59e01cf84908a816f58c50a535f50d0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00014","start":0,"end":120,"exact":"> I was told how in the latest spate of arrests in Jerusalem, a group of young men were blindfolded in an army vehicle. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:916983f1177f49c285b49b951aa98e685fb6258597ba768c6ea03ab1b0fa322a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00014","start":120,"end":212,"exact":"When the ride dragged on, one of them wanted to make sure he's not alone with the soldiers. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:55363c400b61807279f037a8416ffc113f22215edbe23dcee036e0790126ce56","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:8167cd1ad56c98dc70de4ce56500cb10","blockId":"gv-739144-b00014","start":212,"end":304,"exact":"After much thought, he said: “Calm down!” Two responded: “Everything grows clear in plight. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:9589b4ab5fa34ae7326239f60f27cce3","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"9589b4ab5fa34ae7326239f60f27cce3","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:8167cd1ad56c