r":[],"publishedOn":"2021-07-23","sourceUrl":"https://globalvoices.org/2021/07/23/pegasus-spyware-revelation-indicates-indian-state-snooping-on-journalists-activists-and-politicians/","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/","contentSha256":"e440eda93ea4f8eb1775a129650c98dff45655b661fd03f3703ed40a4ebff459","textSha256":"d08226d1e1627a7a5b6a4dfd365c2a13d33d583ace9be5df17fc6344e268b087","archivedRecordSha256":"d66aeda87ff5f7cfea04229ad022ec6c907582c34366342920feaec90b0dc970","inStudy":"urn:doxa:study:muslim-coverage-1"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23:u_2715d76845d97c58a8ed9211","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_2715d76845d97c58a8ed9211","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23:u_a2d497eccbe37b48cb53bb6e","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_a2d497eccbe37b48cb53bb6e","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9bf3cea86d273c7389c2bcc8808176e59569a803af972f678d9a961486cad117","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00013","start":48,"end":242,"exact":"It includes political activists who have been accused of Maoist links who were arrested in 2018 to those who opposed the National Register of Citizens (NRC) and Citizenship Amendment Act (CAA). "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ac683a6943dfa62dd7490209db36d260b32fcdaec2615ddf296ddf89a856c67b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00013","start":242,"end":353,"exact":"Eight of the arrested activists were arrested based on evidence planted on their devices before their arrests. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:05e318cc7dcc4e209bd260782f5fde7ec0841c4742839bd2c022c0cad269d5d4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00013","start":353,"end":525,"exact":"Both CAA and NRC are controversial for their alleged role in the probable displacement of more than 1.9 million residents — mostly minority Muslims — in the state of Assam."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6ae612a24bf7943c6644a88fcbc509339e239cad96b7b28920503fb20b365218","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00014","start":0,"end":123,"exact":"Media outlets that are critical of Modi's ruling Bharatiya Janata Party are seeing a retaliation in the form of tax raids. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:402e991f3d1d6695dec6725f2ee3f5511ed1fba1bdb90c5669c537d95f17073c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00014","start":123,"end":213,"exact":"The noted Hindi-language newspaper Dainik Bhaskar was raided by tax officials on July 22. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6bbf0389e130e2af6818c7a0a5f23ce87fe3249724fe935c3823d35335ee5a48","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00014","start":213,"end":349,"exact":"Dainik Bhaskar not only reported on Pegasus but has persistently questioned the government's choice to downplay COVID-19 related deaths."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:cf00a69b7a7617e35f6ac79cb11a21a4fe32ae9087cc74e72390fafb06a6e465","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00015","start":0,"end":123,"exact":"The Indian government has largely avoided addressing the issue, not confirming whether they purchased and or used Pegasus. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3214b102189ca2d41ddec14599cea8ac86051033d1664313b9456268d1cfd173","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00015","start":123,"end":198,"exact":"An official response claimed that the recent report is based on conjecture:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a7a0c86d53e49dba36ae94b61b6a702209b9e77128a97fb96b8569bf50f7a82f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00016","start":0,"end":132,"exact":"> The allegations regarding government surveillance on specific people has no concrete basis or truth associated with it whatsoever."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e62992316a67d3c58be9a0363d3ab012048d5ab76b3a49acf65cf3ec0469d659","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00017","start":0,"end":160,"exact":"Speaking in Rajya Sabha (the upper house of the Indian parliament), Vaishnaw termed the media reports on the government's link to Pegasus a ‘sensational story’."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ab5ab32ecdb076de8cfe36ce8fc7d24d3b0cbe0db1195cd2ca05a842a0690ae1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00018","start":0,"end":67,"exact":"Journalist Barkha Dutta commented on the situation through Twitter:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d9a342de4e38cf94e1a6be25c2f7682843ccc2712e94f8f19fcffcec60a130a6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00019","start":0,"end":199,"exact":"On July 22, 2021, public interest litigation was filed in the Indian supreme court, seeking a court-monitored probe by a Special Investigation Team into the reports about Pegasus’ intrusion in India."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9fde60bc4027c7db5390056b19797b0bb90abfd5e6f0d007e41d55042f48a42d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00020","start":0,"end":59,"exact":"Hacking devices for surveillance remains illegal in India. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a9cbf2368396b32fa60cbb9e281d8f59fe13ef5cf57bac8e5b5fbd0749205957","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00020","start":59,"end":331,"exact":"Other forms of interception and monitoring are permitted to authorised agencies via the Rule 419A of the Indian Telegraph Rules, 1951, Section 92 in the 1973 Code of Criminal Procedure, Section 69 and 69 B in the 2000 Information Technology Act of the Indian Constitution."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:fe53ac5a0995f51749ca2dfd9354b9132ec9f25448b56197a0862a6eddd89a92","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00021","start":0,"end":184,"exact":"However, as Indian lawyer and co-founder of tech and policy nonprofit the Centre for Internet and Society Pranesh Prakash highlights, there is no clarity about when these rules apply. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4e31122c60dd8d197a61c63ac34e4fcf6906b16cda85ed4a111b3064c6763c46","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00021","start":184,"end":363,"exact":"The Center for Public Interest Litigation and Software Freedom Law Center in Delhi each filed a petition in December 2020 looking to stop several state-run surveillance agencies. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5acad690308db0f66a81491bd58a2a3ef3fd1d84b1c644dafe15ce4821602de4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00021","start":363,"end":427,"exact":"But many forms of rampant surveillance continue in India today. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a10cc6ee6e3a7940b3ba08a1dcbc09f4ade920cb6201e50b5bd16cb4c11f6cfb","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23","blockId":"gv-741671-b00021","start":427,"end":626,"exact":"Indian society is currently grappling with the tensions between government surveillance and citizens’ right to privacy — a guaranteed constitutional right under Article 21 of the Indian Constitution."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:3d5db115e99c61cebb0b0449d68cd729","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"3d5db115e99c61cebb0b0449d68cd729","outcome":"not_applicable","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:95d326e2899f1d220405124ab963fc23:u_2715d76845d97c58a8ed9211","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:9bf3cea86d273c7389c2bcc8808176e59569a803af972f678d9a961486cad117","urn:doxa:passage:ac683a6943dfa62dd7490209db36d260b32fcdaec2615ddf296ddf89a856c67b","urn:doxa:passage:05e318cc7dcc4e209bd260782f5fde7ec0841c4742839bd2c022c0cad269d5d4","urn:doxa:passage:6ae612a24bf7943c6644a88fcbc509339e239cad96b7b28920503fb20b365218","urn:doxa:passage:402e991f3d1d6695dec6725f2ee3f5511ed1fba1bdb90c5669c537d95f17073c","urn:doxa:passage:6bbf0389e130e2af6818c7a0a5f23ce87fe3249724fe935c3823d35335ee5a48","urn:doxa:passage:cf00a69b7a7617e35f6ac79cb11a21a4fe32ae9087cc74e72390fafb06a6e465","urn:doxa:passage:3214b102189ca2d41ddec14599cea8ac86051033d1664313b9456268d1cfd173","urn:doxa:passage:a7a0c86d53e49dba36ae94b61b6a702209b9e77128a97fb96b8569bf50f7a82f","urn:doxa:passage:e62992316a67d3c58be9a0363d3ab012048d5ab76b3a49acf65cf3ec0469d659","urn:doxa:passage:ab5ab32ecdb076de8cfe36ce8fc7d24d3b0cbe0db1195cd2ca05a842a0690ae1","urn:doxa:passage:d9a342de4e38cf94e1a6be25c2f7682843ccc2712e94f8f19fcffcec60a130a6","urn:doxa:passage:9fde60bc4027c7db5390056b19797b0bb90abfd5e6f0d007e41d55042f48a42d","urn:doxa:passage:a9cbf2368396b32fa60cbb9e28