"urn:doxa:passage:a9e4a41e40214ff8106fc2720ffb809fe0a1acb4cde7b80f75a44011fc1df738","urn:doxa:passage:f94843c321cd2162326a93f8250c40be7d37a046ece834f36fb4d7bd28631abd","urn:doxa:passage:e055d5d825475ff93e02cbfa2c1d0ec0f11652197ea37208e0dea13eaf0f1e8e"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d2d20a41b07342b3af5edbf3b3afea00682fc5f0eaa0758f424f94809caa81a8","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00001","start":0,"end":63,"exact":"Welcome to Undertones, the Civic Media Observatory newsletter! "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:431dff24eed292fb03c3afe8aacb6d8e77408d70c22b9127249bd00735a02f63","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00001","start":63,"end":280,"exact":"In each edition we'll analyze an event, emerging trend, or a complex story, identifying key narratives of urgent public interest, delving deep into the context and subtext of local, vernacular and multilingual media. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:01e0b801d57a5aa9ecb030c6974e0ef1c27e94a5a1304da575a75e7114d74a5b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00001","start":280,"end":378,"exact":"Undertones also offers an entry point into the public datasets that underpin our Observatory work."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5d7e4b8ae1c40247f7f8492306f043b5390579e6abfbf7318ac175dd9890acb0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00002","start":0,"end":23,"exact":"Subscribe to Undertones"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:807db90eced6a324fb64e8b827904e85a9c68c1a8eacd32c5a533dcc1d9af99e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00003","start":0,"end":206,"exact":"Russia’s invasion of Ukraine at the end of February coincided with important legislative assembly elections in India, bolstering the expression of expansionist sentiment on the campaign trail and elsewhere."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0651e5f9a5e795e4011b761678b8663712da809c842e2f657cfd1c7f19b53302","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00004","start":0,"end":123,"exact":"Expansionist narratives have long been present in Indian media, but the war in Ukraine has given them an additional boost. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7d5db499138963fd9e328819b1370341cb7956c58d3c0f4aeb84d271fa99954a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00004","start":123,"end":356,"exact":"Now that legislative assembly elections are over, with the ruling Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) having won major states—setting the tone for India’s 2024 general elections—pro-BJP media are seeking to humiliate and silence dissenters."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d13297d40966d40bccde27a4834cc1d7082bee06c9284903fb1d967aa69a4f17","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00005","start":0,"end":201,"exact":"The BJP and hyper-nationalist Hindutva groups have also used the war to position Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi as an indispensable global leader and promote the establishment of a “United India.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1a4e88415c0d3af6203e1ce1adaf7ade66f8d4c1cbea82afeda0b905c41d54bc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00006","start":0,"end":99,"exact":"Diplomatically, India has remained neutral with regard to the conflict between Russia and Ukraine. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2abe303350dd95767fd2c00724da7d92582f678c46c1201d19520fd5db6c29c1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00006","start":99,"end":221,"exact":"Within the country’s borders, however, mainstream media and far-right groups have expressed support for Putin’s invasion. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6d926177e5c44efb4b782c3ed7c11713d08c7db5a8a71d63b62e932cedb73330","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00006","start":221,"end":569,"exact":"Not only is Russia India’s oldest and most strategic partner, but Putin’s expansionist ideology bears striking similarities to the hyper-nationalism of one of the key concepts of Hindutva: “Akhand Bharat” or “One India,” and commentators are drawing parallels between the breakdown of the Soviet Union and the division of India after colonial rule."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:083bf81631acbe206d914b859965c07d88c6b830f8b0d7541d46426a6adb033c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00007","start":0,"end":20,"exact":"Dangerous narratives"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b32ccc6014015535865ba6da652e3ad7c33da63c4bb4cdf7248aa3decb7b0bb1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00008","start":0,"end":144,"exact":"Such narratives are prevalent on high-engagement extremist Hindutva Facebook pages and unverified news media outlets operating on social media. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c29f198087154576a19d37f251db2da9c940b326ae800561ba893a900d80fc45","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00008","start":144,"end":229,"exact":"They can also be found on BJP-aligned broadcast media, albeit in a more subtle form. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f8873f24aa6301736b0f6e57dad9d586447948c59465bca01cb51cc143774a34","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00008","start":229,"end":384,"exact":"Canned expressions of pro-BJP sentiment – such as “hail Modi” – showing up in the comments section below social media posts appear to be the work of bots. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:bb3bce288cab8d655809034b21211e8eeace1eaf47f6b727f75f9869ff77ea74","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00008","start":384,"end":545,"exact":"There have been allegations that mega-conglomerate Reliance Industries is funding a firm that promotes pro-BJP advertisements and false news stories on Facebook."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:16b66161235e059f3e530287ffd149e1264392252806dd46d3ee361255b0688b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00009","start":0,"end":63,"exact":"1) “The whole of the Jammu and Kashmir region belongs to India”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:385a6d347b9afab28e04636f2afbecf142f193f0e58a570b82c4de86b4261809","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00010","start":0,"end":269,"exact":"Since Russia invaded Ukraine on February 24, Indian social media has been buzzing with tweets and memes demanding that India’s Prime Minister Narendra Modi take advantage of the world’s preoccupation with Ukraine to mimic Putin and annex Kashmir and other territories. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:11fff9d12288a4efa8ca0b32df45967064d022540b7a6bfed00f3410a320be66","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00010","start":269,"end":400,"exact":"According to this narrative, India’s ally, Russia, is setting an example of “state reunification,” and the West is not stopping it."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2cdff34c1dc4fc0a6b08c83b12aaf6bc6b21d407613dd78ceb1cbe96fe84c8e8","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00011","start":0,"end":96,"exact":"The Kashmir valley is a disputed area claimed by India, Pakistan, and the Kashmiris themselves. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4143a1c47d6bf6037aaec4a0281a71e802c054178da88053aa9d884d1a02f34f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00011","start":96,"end":224,"exact":"When India gained independence in 1947, its largely Muslim-populated territories were carved out to form the state of Pakistan. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:bbbdab4566ce28a638bd10f9f1d059011cdd7a7f8bb6f818606e36a3272c6f92","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00011","start":224,"end":395,"exact":"Kashmir was the exception and was eventually divided into Indian-administered Kashmir and Pakistan-administered Kashmir, called “Pakistan Occupied Kashmir” (PoK) in India."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:75a22d614f0564480507cd2448b93423a838841ef8d8f825c82465ce11c8c1e2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00012","start":0,"end":156,"exact":"While Kashmiris await a UN-supported referendum that would grant them the right to choose their future, BJP leaders have vowed to take over all of Kashmir. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9e99a9a7bb1cd9e0506037b6647bec1eeb5916c7f45a7cfa49f6489c6c984c78","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00012","start":156,"end":252,"exact":"India’s 2019 dissolution of Jammu and Kashmir’s statehood was an initial step in that direction."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d6946133a870d28729edb0f96576139c55b0f3b14207ec72429f18bb6d8c45f0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00013","start":0,"end":106,"exact":"Video on Facebook: “The world is busy in the Russia-Ukraine conflict and Modiji has made his move on PoK?”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6b2ee2370e57ac0e6336cd391c7911542207593a0177fbf397236d495fb94f89","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00014","start":0,"end":165,"exact":"The item, which received half a million views, is an interview with a politics expert who states that India should follow the example of Russia and attack Pakistan. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2e9ecaec663abbbd7232a71034063e8df33c832b2c28e0de5c8314c3f93e2d2c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00014","start":165,"end":444,"exact":"India should “grant independence” to the Pakistani provinces of Sindh and Balochistan, and annex “Pakistan Occupied Kashmir.” The item claims that other countries have done nothing to stop the Ukraine war, and they will similarly not stop India if it decides to attack Pakistan. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:94c213f3ee1b6b9e7f039f4f5eb9c462","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"94c213f3ee1b6b9e7f039f4f5eb9c462","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8:u_547c86702df0e76c692efb88","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:d2d20a41b07342b3af5edbf3b3afea00682fc5f0eaa0758f424f94809caa81a8","urn:doxa:passage:431dff24eed292fb03c3afe8aacb6d8e77408d70c22b9127249bd00735a02f63","urn:doxa:passage:01e0b801d57a5aa9ecb030