b4261809","urn:doxa:passage:11fff9d12288a4efa8ca0b32df45967064d022540b7a6bfed00f3410a320be66","urn:doxa:passage:2cdff34c1dc4fc0a6b08c83b12aaf6bc6b21d407613dd78ceb1cbe96fe84c8e8","urn:doxa:passage:4143a1c47d6bf6037aaec4a0281a71e802c054178da88053aa9d884d1a02f34f","urn:doxa:passage:bbbdab4566ce28a638bd10f9f1d059011cdd7a7f8bb6f818606e36a3272c6f92","urn:doxa:passage:75a22d614f0564480507cd2448b93423a838841ef8d8f825c82465ce11c8c1e2","urn:doxa:passage:9e99a9a7bb1cd9e0506037b6647bec1eeb5916c7f45a7cfa49f6489c6c984c78","urn:doxa:passage:d6946133a870d28729edb0f96576139c55b0f3b14207ec72429f18bb6d8c45f0","urn:doxa:passage:6b2ee2370e57ac0e6336cd391c7911542207593a0177fbf397236d495fb94f89","urn:doxa:passage:2e9ecaec663abbbd7232a71034063e8df33c832b2c28e0de5c8314c3f93e2d2c"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:175ff5aee17d8deba8fe1b107054d6e45cfe005f799109fa4470996b136cbbb1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00014","start":444,"end":526,"exact":"The interview was conducted by “The Newspaper TV,” which operates on social media."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:667ec621a96adac35e670b8432658930b5f660a1a0117d107198464e45a74725","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00015","start":0,"end":178,"exact":"See more analysis of this media item here and other items showcasing this narrative, including those dating from before Ukraine’s invasion: IN_164, IN 236, IN_268, IN_272, IN_305"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ecc709495697d11d4ef7e88fa841c69131e702e0e5d3f02c51399620eff29197","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00016","start":0,"end":84,"exact":"2) “India should emulate Russia and pursue the goal of United India (Akhand Bharat)”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1434bad8bf36e4fe84a556067fc941cc0d6fbea1e6f8726c315bc4c2ba836efc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00017","start":0,"end":83,"exact":"This narrative arose as a result of Russia’s invasion of Ukraine in February 2022. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9082b157ee18dc90d4d95986701268abbf50043e6657115f93b1dd072c9c3b36","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00017","start":83,"end":281,"exact":"Hindutva groups have shown support for Putin, claiming that the Russian leader’s aspiration to create a new USSR, or Russian empire, are similar to the Hindutva ambition to create a “United India”. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:565c17f08988d9c95fe649e0b1bcaca32c1e5cfb132d67c32093dfa161123bb9","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00017","start":281,"end":346,"exact":"This narrative is broader than the previous one and builds on it."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:55019f6d6b1988c7cef2b8868653b535f85cffdce3668ea3eec9398cd965b5ad","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00018","start":0,"end":122,"exact":"The concept of “Akhand Bharat” (“One India” or “United India”) is among the key tenets of the Hindu nationalist movement. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7f11de2b5a2d1182fee3eb86229e0fa19087f0d5b884751ca54a2a6b20bc9882","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00018","start":122,"end":256,"exact":"Hindutva groups, therefore, openly celebrate the ideological similarity with Putin and express support for his expansionist ambitions."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f42618f58ee086d3321cffae3b42c96daba1a87cc52092cbabc00b41ae8b62b4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00019","start":0,"end":148,"exact":"Many Hindutva supporters have also gone so far as to demand that India attack Pakistan and return India to its pre-independence geographical state. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:95e46eaa7bb86a063f49dda403c65f00b13cb39ce2ba3047546c418692186d9a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00019","start":148,"end":361,"exact":"For them, Russia has a legitimate claim over Ukraine as a former Soviet state, as does India over Pakistan, as formerly a part of India, along with other South Asian countries such as Bangladesh, Tibet, and Nepal."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8fa9e83cb7ad01f90c878d7066133bcb4f71dd3598a599db18171dbd5f19998b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00020","start":0,"end":43,"exact":"Meme: “Putin started project Akhand Russia”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2ee37ed1d2e61ca8843d59b99f8190d8c585112cdf2118075fa7ea2ef4a02105","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00021","start":0,"end":551,"exact":"This meme superimposes a photo of Vladimir Putin’s face on the body of Yogi Adityanath, a prominent BJP politician, along with the caption “Putin started project Akhand Russia,” drawing parallels between Putin’s attempt to “unite Russian” by conquering a former Soviet republic and the vision of “Akhand Bharat” or “One India.” Yogi Adityanth is a proponent of Hindutva and is a member of the RSS, an organization pushing for the creation of Akhand Bharat and the “reuniting” South Asian countries that were divided after and during the colonial era. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ca3848765d2ccbfec5e871ee4fc5f9ec038054d8b6283d802474af368e9f115f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00021","start":551,"end":612,"exact":"This meme has been shared in Whatsapp groups and on Facebook."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:cdbd44cfced378bc346f1147b9902e57649fbbe1a1a8d18741fe679a1e782b0b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00022","start":0,"end":99,"exact":"See more analysis of this media item here and other items showcasing this narrative: IN_287, IN_291"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:476ee55922dd46efe2ff32e7417ae9c20f64f18340f8d829e305c55947cf0576","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00023","start":0,"end":90,"exact":"3) “India's global prestige and power has increased under the leadership of Narendra Modi”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:75a897c72c25220678b21a993ab4200b93fe3a10217ee27ab2232209f3cf2e38","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00024","start":0,"end":140,"exact":"When the BJP government came to power in India in 2014, Prime Minister Narendra Modi promised to lead India in becoming a world superpower. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:346d5c489dc214a24865a6fb71313ae7cd42e22c5c0382e331f81e929dc6c7e1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00024","start":140,"end":231,"exact":"For the BJP and pro-Modi groups, that opportunity presented itself with the war in Ukraine."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:fc54ddd12938ca6ffc80fe69ed92cb143363a583007404154c506d5f324dcb31","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00025","start":0,"end":335,"exact":"In general, Modi is seen as a superhero by his followers, but since Russia invaded Ukraine, memes and posts by right-wing groups have promoted the vision of Modi as a powerful “alpha male” or “Vishwa Guru” (“World Leader”) who is capable of stopping the war, especially as Ukrainian diplomat Igor Polikha has requested India’s support."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a3ea7850577de08ca41d338d1122e4d69d0a1c493489632cd7f3aebbb6d43f93","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00026","start":0,"end":142,"exact":"In broadcast media, too, Modi was hailed as a global leader and savior following the controversial evacuation of Indian students from Ukraine."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:517267f34d6879aad0077931a9fc47848b6b93e7bf7f0f304edf350c24860ee8","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00027","start":0,"end":90,"exact":"Pro-Modi media cannot be examined in isolation from state legislative assembly elections. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:26425e627adf00e29cef1a31b0b657325eacf1576ae3ed338af311aaaddbac05","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00027","start":90,"end":278,"exact":"At a time when Modi has been criticized for rising anti-Muslim violence in India, media reports have tried to whitewash his image by portraying him as a strong and necessary global leader."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a4d363a7ba58a53326966de29be4d32d961c1d3a8a133287973d101cb3fa506d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00028","start":0,"end":87,"exact":"Video on Facebook: “The whole world is astonished as to why Putin only listens to Modi”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:60cd1c607d0441ac91e0c51615c30d85abb54e1df5b7cd3f472d14d72b41c292","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00029","start":0,"end":161,"exact":"Unverified online news channel “NIO TIMES” shared a Facebook video that glorifies Putin and argues that the West is powerless before Russia and India’s leaders. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:cc6e90267aed82fbc757acfcdcd9c9be6dfd52093e1907cd00473a80719a0231","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00029","start":161,"end":252,"exact":"Since Putin and Modi’s alliance threatens the West, they have used Ukraine to bait Russia. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d12f3b77df894206b7bade596671f8c8ee1afa2141c841e197929ac7d7be119a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00029","start":252,"end":367,"exact":"The item concludes by saying that Narendra Modi can prevent a global catastrophe by convincing Putin to calm down. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:334bbf3ba5319253a662518a3c429f2dc36517dba1a687918fd8586b2b1f0666","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00029","start":367,"end":443,"exact":"The item, which garnered 179k likes, implies that India must support Russia."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5a6c652d1bf45791c318011e4b94f9b6e56d0a1b0fe84cd6adb785debd79ba68","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00030","start":0,"end":207,"exact":"See more analysis of this media item here and other items showcasing this narrative, including those hailing Modi’s government for evacuating Indian students: IN_282, IN_295, IN_296, IN_305, IN_310, IN_313. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6ae30d7a496da9a33566a8a3e7f5b22fc53ec736d9e3407cddf492b53b361787","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:61ae8b482ee6d1a7c22d8f553d9a22a8","blockId":"gv-758849-b00030","start":207,"end":310,"exact":"Also, here is an analysis of Twitter thread by an independent journalist mocking this narrative: IN_264"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:324866f5fd3a2ef8cd2006fe6aa7b054","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],