sage:3384ea55fcacaec80e829c669c03380cd329809c0b6bc994bf8adc0eaf272f54","urn:doxa:passage:25a52606e57146daf4040559b7a1b7189f4cc53a194faca1bf26ae0a9391442b"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0b8caf30a1ac98b08ede7c5c59887a65827ad5038f5950cd9061f9be8e8c3c51","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00001","start":0,"end":108,"exact":"When people in Uzbekistan get information about China, their perception is shaped by the media they follow. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9a4b35753dd26e90825969875ddba1e6e7c2750e632404bea4403379dcae969f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00001","start":108,"end":247,"exact":"While some worry about Uzbekistan’s increasing external debt to China; others perceive their giant neighbour as a useful economic partner. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:305f2072ab5f951ca36c4fed7295eeeaa099689f3e2ff4ae79e87dbc3ff37958","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00001","start":247,"end":368,"exact":"And some, usually more religious, strongly condemn China’s attitude towards the Uyghurs and consider it a foe of Muslims."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8be6250cbdb76803ab83da60c5379d9d39de67fefd1076f8c8673f15767118e0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00002","start":0,"end":161,"exact":"Since the beginning of the Belt and Road Initiative, China’s relations with the countries of Central Asia, including Uzbekistan, have strengthened to new level. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:468133f70d558d94f1a40e1b574b797d99a07e1f5a0bebe5a95a593550b27164","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00002","start":161,"end":284,"exact":"According to official data, the volume of trade between Uzbekistan and China has increased 140 times in the last 30 years. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e240fd364c567efb665259b5907677f89ddadf0348f2be85c24cf28c9709c87d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00002","start":284,"end":374,"exact":"Since 2017, the size of Chinese investment in the Uzbek economy has increased five times. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e0d44f020ac1ac9f09629b207fc0c1b8b0d1c9c7297b300a6663a7681ab9205a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00002","start":374,"end":556,"exact":"From 2017 to the start of the pandemic in early 2020, leading officials of all 14 regions of Uzbekistan have been invited to and visited various provinces and large cities of China. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f3902054e33ffc56b5972cfec224ecbc32da59604ae25c41d1c665d78e8dbcd4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00002","start":556,"end":650,"exact":"As a result, China has maintained its position as one of Uzbekistan's biggest trade partners. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a0bc402a5ca5cbe948584e1e0866cf35d22a61be7694c25e621c09edfc22e5d0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00002","start":650,"end":703,"exact":"Also, it remains Uzbekistan's largest export market. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ba196f211eb00c1f5ce5e625e36e1320abb12f6361858763d9772950e8c8ae2a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00002","start":703,"end":848,"exact":"But, despite the fact that economic and political relations are moving only upwards, the image of China in the Uzbek media space remains complex."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:18f448579fb0bd0fe9cc918b1f566b00ff5c5f21da3be5ee46bd313bb001038b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00003","start":0,"end":49,"exact":"China as a friend in state-controlled Uzbek media"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7052fb9d5be5b7dac946fc0c5ad79113eaef39cc16c9c6bc922b321245fd953f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00004","start":0,"end":73,"exact":"State-controlled media still dominate the media landscape in Uzbekistan. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:25efff96eaf7c0998a58643280bf9217353e51a3e5cfcb587532b25ece054537","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00004","start":73,"end":275,"exact":"Global Voices analyzed the coverage of China by the National Information Agency of Uzbekistan Uza.uz , the official, state-owned media agency, which is also the country’s leading official news website. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:06c73d123f437c568507d578ed0128d1d30f456698381afc28795ef5230d418f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00004","start":275,"end":456,"exact":"Most news (about 44 percent of the total related to China) on this website in 2021–2022 includes political news, with a focus on China–Russia, China–USA and China–Taiwan relations. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9cd420b04b26807c1b7745ff27870c110a23e03da0c066f85c27517ea21fb126","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00004","start":456,"end":633,"exact":"Interestingly, Uza.uz’s coverage included numerous articles about China’s good relations with Russia, and achievements in the strategic partnership between these two countries. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6546313af1403af815f7de0c3930ce88b1624cfa4ecf20818dd67355068bd05c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00004","start":633,"end":752,"exact":"In contrast, only conflictual and problematic situations were highlighted when covering China’s relations with the US. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1081bbd2d18dbb16da8b6744fe1b136e13ae973bd388bae5bf6685c346826501","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00004","start":752,"end":990,"exact":"A closer look at the original sources of the news reveals that they are direct references to Russian media outlets such as TASS (a major Russian state-owned news agency) and Ria Novosti (another Russian state-owned domestic news agency). "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:62eba1768dc5be7725eff1aedccb3f81568b84dbbb3eb698b03f57943bf77359","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00004","start":990,"end":1093,"exact":"Additionally, Uza.uz has less news coverage about Taiwan and Uyghurs than other more independent sites."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f5b1ff9865bda8b8343be003df544b33d193f3997d2cecac9d755269bd5be9a7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00005","start":0,"end":185,"exact":"The second biggest category of news in the period — 29 percent — focused on the good relationship between Uzbekistan and China, new political and economic deals and cultural exchanges. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:58cbf36634c3baf02c541a2eae3ded706c90bc55d6c416efbf737e351b27b0cb","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00005","start":185,"end":293,"exact":"In this case, China is presented as a good strategic partner, as in the following example from May 25, 2022:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:aa11c252ac8a9e3aaff6448f0d56127f97ff48f0398c6086b168bbf1a9ed2961","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00006","start":0,"end":285,"exact":"> Хитой ҳукумати Ўзбекистонга 250 миллион юань маблағ ажратди. Битим Хитой Халқ Республикаси томонидан Ўзбекистон Республикасида ижтимоий аҳамиятга молик лойиҳаларни биргаликда амалга ошириш учун 250 миллион юань (37,5 миллион доллар) миқдорида беғараз ёрдам кўрсатишни назарда тутади."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7748bd915393d9b7f817d0976e2b056fd85d8008a84be120fcbcaf6d031cffd4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00007","start":0,"end":67,"exact":"> The Chinese government allocated 250 million yuan to Uzbekistan. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2cde56b6b6890ecc4bd80b7eed4f5465f6a3d8f545ad1d8534d36d56ff746518","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00007","start":67,"end":286,"exact":"The agreement envisages the provision of 250 million yuan ($37.5 million) in kind assistance by the People's Republic of China for the joint implementation of socially significant projects in the Republic of Uzbekistan."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f3bef8b859bec5930502e20a61a387981db7a113094ddb05c29308043fe1c057","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00008","start":0,"end":281,"exact":"When it comes to television, which is still the most popular source of media, especially among the older generation and in sub-urban and rural regions, news about China mostly covers soft topics, typically focusing on Chinese culture, history, geography and advanced technologies. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4fbe898357ad82238743e4fc2c0ac6b4c6d0781970324b2c34b1072e1fc34ea6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00008","start":281,"end":352,"exact":"There is almost no news touching upon politically controversial issues."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c4d08303cd58112ce26ba2473e091e1733868ca0aa08cb9871457b603db19f66","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00009","start":0,"end":212,"exact":"This comes as no surprise: official media in Central Asian countries is often criticised for its high-sounding rhetoric and pro-government context, and it does not cover most politically sensitive news as a rule."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e7d40ccebe1638fd7d53613402d5a3f3381cd8a4bc1b135b040e62a47f56e7e2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00010","start":0,"end":56,"exact":"Independent media paint a more nuanced portrait of China"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:279fd9fad8aadf66653033a86e1f174ffdcc0e1d36f43b55149308a8e9ce965a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00011","start":0,"end":143,"exact":"The media sector in Uzbekistan has gained some autonomy since 2016, when the new President Shavkat Mirziyoyev started a wide range of reforms. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:ae0cfd376da6afa38554525aa21c47ce","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"ae0cfd376da6afa38554525aa21c47ce","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77:u_c06ecd80985b9160b8712995","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:p