:"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00021","start":229,"end":429,"exact":"The appalling conditions, torture and sexual harassment alleged to be practiced in the so-called “morality camps” by the Chinese government have been shaking the internet news space for some time now."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d1dcbe4d08e93611ac7a105726c031fe734e9b53f90d2873d0ee337540ae61a3","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00022","start":0,"end":103,"exact":"Nevertheless, in recent years, some influencers and bloggers have put forth a positive image of China. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:10975de502240dd786bfe1c9757b372c743cbe3ba6920829fdf8b9742b25a568","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00022","start":103,"end":333,"exact":"This is mainly due to increasing Chinese investment and businesses in Uzbekistan, China’s economic and technological advancements, and partially because of the impact of the ongoing war between Russia and Ukraine on Central Asia. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:32fc7f04c8740dbd1be965e04cd1bbcb6566bfd64c6723b309759af3e5f0fd3e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00022","start":333,"end":494,"exact":"In particular, Uzbekistan's investment and trade agreements with China amounting to USD 15 billion during the SCO-2022 summit have been praised by some bloggers."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:475353cbae73fac47aeb828e8db660669207c7954780cd3ad3d1a6a2d3740467","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00023","start":0,"end":198,"exact":"In a nutshell, China’s image can be seen in various tones on different sources of media in Uzbekistan, and people’s perceptions of it are mostly shaped by the media source they refer to frequently. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b41d9a3d51ee349e038d2b524ac9f2b3bd8e4ac4af8affffca95e6ba48a8a215","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77","blockId":"gv-775348-b00023","start":198,"end":426,"exact":"With the increase of China’s engagement in international geopolitics and in Central Asia, there is going to be more interest in and heated discussions about China in Uzbekistan, and such discussions are getting more politicized."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:da93960f451a0054131cd13763149cfb","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"da93960f451a0054131cd13763149cfb","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:31cea45e671b55e4cd205d98160faf77:u_ff2e530a731dd2ae91195fe6","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:35860df209e507fcd852f780787d602b8d3d34c005c34b927c6f47ca4dc5519f","urn:doxa:passage:e737564da40e04f2711b46a2891007652ee77aa2e7e14acdc8f8ee7d53b9a71c","urn:doxa:passage:d1dcbe4d08e93611ac7a105726c031fe734e9b53f90d2873d0ee337540ae61a3","urn:doxa:passage:10975de502240dd786bfe1c9757b372c743cbe3ba6920829fdf8b9742b25a568","urn:doxa:passage:32fc7f04c8740dbd1be965e04cd1bbcb6566bfd64c6723b309759af3e5f0fd3e","urn:doxa:passage:475353cbae73fac47aeb828e8db660669207c7954780cd3ad3d1a6a2d3740467","urn:doxa:passage:b41d9a3d51ee349e038d2b524ac9f2b3bd8e4ac4af8affffca95e6ba48a8a215"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:6f6384a7bdf71becade65aa6b9b7b7c9","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"6f6384a7bdf71becade65aa6b9b7b7c9","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca704712