eneration-be-after-the-war-in-ukraine/","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/","contentSha256":"8b3ac784894ce923e0c476f976375d1843d7f2b41720f2f373fd3adb47fa3780","textSha256":"ed6baa6b9d6cf1c6852c90cad618495a0191c74524b543cd9ac7f8c780d08ef5","archivedRecordSha256":"9fa0811fd3a6391644042dd58775bc25d8b4dafe32ff438698e2443d41e9892c","inStudy":"urn:doxa:study:muslim-coverage-1"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8:u_0630b0cc7a13e69e795df055","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_0630b0cc7a13e69e795df055","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8:u_88b8fdca8149d9ea8fc0c386","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_88b8fdca8149d9ea8fc0c386","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8:u_d42033fd8eccb01eeffa3fb9","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_d42033fd8eccb01eeffa3fb9","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:092b81e39fd753b4cdaafa049af21015a8180ebbd8519f1dd740caed5b7dc160","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00007","start":819,"end":1050,"exact":"We survived the Chernobyl disaster, the poverty of the 1990s, perestroika, the dangerous temptations of the first years of independence, the revolution, and the emergence of ourselves as individuals in an era of continuous change. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:800c410a43f66d41654d5505ce2c52b551e5fdcafd69009356ab832bf6105324","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00007","start":1050,"end":1069,"exact":"Now we are at war. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e6964313a21dd95d6813ce72acdc0182733b0b6c80e304c9fe458d010d3fb457","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00007","start":1069,"end":1105,"exact":"This is no longer an era of change. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0ee5a5cdf624b7804c5c6d33533f0d1c0533e292f7e8d4cdb30caf452c19c490","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00007","start":1105,"end":1210,"exact":"This is a radical transition of another level, and my generation is bearing the brunt of this transition."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4f59a9c2673c31f607154b1f7c0aafc48ec54ac7175a9bd9d2f1b6205d9f44c0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00008","start":0,"end":145,"exact":"In December 2021, I interviewed many of my Kyiv acquaintances trying to understand how they were experiencing the emerging threat at the border. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e36e9ab1d707f93b127a7ba2a2d7bb1922080f69bd9f2531c3213d33edaf6727","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00008","start":145,"end":199,"exact":"Under the guise of peace, there was anxiety and fear. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6f3e9f09517c1c18dc8f6dee324eef40b7e217ce7b1676792261d0bd14ff65b9","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00008","start":199,"end":317,"exact":"Everyone was sick with fear about the imminent attack of Kyiv; many packed grab bags; they made plans in case of war. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:35d89c08b9368b3c0538a223fe6aa47a4aa8d50803cb16f5cc602346cdc05878","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00008","start":317,"end":346,"exact":"What steps should they take? "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:53f0f5227213a36da409adb0e01676078d75b5df7ca985e7cd8769abb29fbf06","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00008","start":346,"end":352,"exact":"Flee? "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:20e4201c1346c9aeaa7889755307b47ee31ab9b2effe7166b921a0f548db0eaf","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00008","start":352,"end":385,"exact":"Save their parents and children? "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5bc0487f3f2f7211e4355a1dae95f9fcd88d0da05747caeb0ffa914943cf53d0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00008","start":385,"end":396,"exact":"Go to war? "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ed72f28878d1bc1db99126fc4b2e1b4e2f7f883ae3c6b4cc31389a62fcd4b348","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00008","start":396,"end":437,"exact":"Or wait for someone else to act for you? "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4323889da80f023d1782d4e5b81db89373a6a9dbe78e4f1d8b1bfa6be89be8bb","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00008","start":437,"end":543,"exact":"What is happening, and is it worth planning new projects, books, or trips abroad for January and February?"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5bd3383ca464e0b70881174f628fb1e0090a988a8eb444a49465903aebc59008","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00009","start":0,"end":183,"exact":"Looking back at history, we should have predicted that the Kremlin would indeed again sacrifice hundreds of thousands of their citizens for the sake of their distorted utopian goals. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:dec74d42010acf1c7badce618051978e5f4df928e0b6ce5a6fe56825f577d3ae","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00009","start":183,"end":348,"exact":"We should have known that they would decimate residential neighborhoods with artillery and allow punitive units of murderers and marauders into the occupied cities. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e5543bef2bb39a9502793307f2fdcd81eec64c4af1d69666eaad3a5411e23706","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00009","start":348,"end":456,"exact":"Russia has never cared for human resources, and it is unlikely that anything has changed in recent decades. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e8ead10bd2664366ef916c45a1f2c39e02edc6a76c6a4cb0f3c08b480b1d4471","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00009","start":456,"end":499,"exact":"There is only one question left: the cost. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7d3fb72c2ad37ba3795168338dfd8b8c17164949eb78829f8efa36df207d9a91","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00009","start":499,"end":538,"exact":"What sacrifices is Putin ready to make?"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:00dedff714baf570e38777da13e8cf4699db53ffba2c5502b89cba5d8974e4f1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00010","start":0,"end":54,"exact":"Ukrainian people had a lot of questions of their own. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:56b15bb514012ef23123be84c562fd8921724e8eb2c138a6cc6595da55f2fb45","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00010","start":54,"end":182,"exact":"The most important question was, “Who of us will go to defend the land and the loved ones?” Eventually, some people stepped up. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1bf599f8f3d0193fcd3ae9c58950ce1ab8bfaaa19d98dd4f4852827ff437b1ff","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00010","start":182,"end":280,"exact":"There are many very young soldiers, but the backbone of the army consists of us, 30–40-year-olds. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:21041162888d622ab834c7f81ebe0a7ea53621b2c4ca86fb95f8728765c6353d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00010","start":280,"end":471,"exact":"A generation that has generally grown up on the same Russian culture, with a misguidedly concrete conviction of their own provincial second-classness and a quiet envy of civilized countries. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:aeeab62a849e047bceb074f27df5155ae729a3d3cf8abeffc27d9c755726fa77","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00010","start":471,"end":710,"exact":"Although we arrived at our patriotism for Ukrainian from different paths, we all realized we had a duty to protect our territories, our not-always-integral-identity, and our not-always-native-language, but we reached a common denominator. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b9d92e656a8e41287a1c33b7c562ab6620b25279f73417439c117197a74325ae","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00010","start":710,"end":779,"exact":"We are a generation of Ukrainians who united for the sake of victory."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b162e4f45538e722126297020607380dc6e865333a2a54477c359a82fa4aebc0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":0,"end":43,"exact":"I keep thinking about when I was 17 or 18. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1e4889893e428dd888aa59bb3784961ed1b13e73125162fc0e1ea4bdeeadeab1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":43,"end":108,"exact":"At that time, I was not at all interested in Ukrainian politics. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:cfab7dface50beb62bc684b60ff2ac65b50c8227af12cb333bb6c9f1d8837a7c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":108,"end":204,"exact":"The Orange Revolution that I was actively involved in during my student years had not come yet. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f251744fdbfb1383b834356d0f2db8694426526a5a740e9147e894bf0902b0b5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":204,"end":301,"exact":"Almost my whole childhood and adolescence unfolded under the poverty of Kuchma's stagnation era. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:01aeb918395a1c409c9f32ba3c3c2e6b99a9a8893c8719470360550ab1643815","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":301,"end":339,"exact":"It seemed like it would last forever. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:babab5a9d64fec7e07dfc49a4b6370bdbf12e9cb52df7e9dbfadfa485fea6518","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":339,"end":428,"exact":"The nineties ended in a fun way, with drunken teenage shrieks and the taste of lipstick. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3702c4ffa9b3fb704929722cd953f751e2e42528e82dbd46b7d55f527a307270","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":428,"end":479,"exact":"A new life began in a hopelessly stagnant country. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:778f715105e10004f7d4486e95535f605bfbe0101786340de103096e62b6c988","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":479,"end":508,"exact":"But I didn't think about it. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5c181ba8370bc4203af8b6aca750c60bffc71487c003fc72cfc25ded207a16e1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":508,"end":537,"exact":"I thought of something else. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b1c689d2840eb7564ebcc9754c517ce2ac3c13bf731eac9c19a98c8cc1048aaa","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":537,"end":609,"exact":"I⁠ thought of Ukraine being a periphery of Europe, a quiet swampy pond. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:73e60e60c902fbd2f834f90c834cc04d7e06a83553931197282ce813dda2f026","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":609,"end":709,"exact":"It was not interested in anyone; no one was interested in it; and war was the least of its worries. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:454c26d378497db9290dc160fc281073dcd9f1c4826570d619b3464046edf345","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":709,"end":774,"exact":"Oddly enough, I had been thinking a lot about wars at that time. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:52b18fe6bc12271bc327bea92f42936edb768b8d50bdd167cb90a84327e47ce0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":774,"end":825,"exact":"The Second Chechen War, Kosovo, Afghanistan, Iraq. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:fcc6669a952db3ecb066a5de88abfcaa09a555e8e241cdad15c195ba26d9686c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":825,"end":904,"exact":"Something terrible was happening outside of my world, outside of common sense. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:55eb4c821fa04d533416d6dfcd604e7a3ecd76a273f60eddfa76c6b0258ed3ee","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":904,"end":987,"exact":"The attacks could have occurred in Russia, Ireland, Spain, or in Muslim countries. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7268924ba65fe1a7876f7f7c6f6c83570aa7cda8bf2a95a563aceff216fa9838","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":987,"end":1040,"exact":"Torture chambers were deployed in African countries. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8ab826aed5f7ec8968ed4540b75b5b60cb54f27cc34a90c36d667fd166289a9b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00011","start":1040,"end":1229,"exact":"The only peak our conflicts reached was the protest campaign “Ukraine without Kuchma.” For me, it went almost unnoticed as, I say again, politics was the last thing I cared about back then."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b170713c3c7c5a0e45ef620c471baddac564c0c99c7e6f7384e446f5c7ad0011","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00012","start":0,"end":92,"exact":"And now I am sitting deep in the woods, wearing military pants and a National Guard jacket. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c5c0ba31af0f26db59912c1db49ab433f8024b138b87b442fc05a495d5c9f66f","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00012","start":92,"end":194,"exact":"I am 37, and I have a bunch of written books under my belt, also translations, depression, and a gun. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e009c48b7750bb74cf54133a13fa01aba8426d4ea25e5e9d9ae7ef43739840a9","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00012","start":194,"end":224,"exact":"My country is fighting a war. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1aafb96901838a45837ed0231c5e58d9aae73ac7d15a445f8e04d5cd92fc869b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00012","start":224,"end":263,"exact":"It is real, big, ruthless, and bloody. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a004e764a343fb003706925cd57ccce8f7c6babe42d884e22da5745e137fa993","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00012","start":263,"end":326,"exact":"And I am a soldier in this war, one of those who took up arms. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6daece7906cd5dc48ad11c59492bf6033bee2e56226ed2d87e52795bec84e095","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00012","start":326,"end":347,"exact":"And my weapon kills. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2844607b4c1d11917206b1d18da330a64c7b3590d706412dedc3e8159a68dffb","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00012","start":347,"end":368,"exact":"It kills my enemies. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8b3fa3feeebcc3793a8423d4aecfedfa685785d65cc5aff4dcaa4fb98aaa375c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:400fa8599e639ce8e5cc16adb1831ee8","blockId":"gv-788705-b00012","start":368,"end":461,"exact":"It all sounds simple and matter-of-fact — as if this has been the reality for all our lives. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:fa3dc5c7cab64f06d47cc4596cfd767c","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"fa3dc5c7cab64f06d47cc4596cfd767c","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operation