rn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00002","start":85,"end":240,"exact":"This week, Turkish researcher Sencer Odabaşi breaks down what the conversations are like on Turkish Twitter following the reelection of President Erdoğan. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c7e4bc08b07ba735cd1f7c55b9d6595fa087a69e47d1676916fbf2374b3fdad7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00002","start":240,"end":300,"exact":"Some of the most vivid reactions are aimed at LGBTQ+ groups."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0ffee8d576c0761de3b606bd598a666704d2bf68a059c7caae971ea4cc03ae0c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00003","start":0,"end":147,"exact":"On June 25, LGBTQ+ groups and individuals will march through the streets of Istanbul, Turkey, fully aware that they may encounter police violence. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a5e92dd2e6d5b9384b00a6409effe5d12e3e4dfd67e6dd96e398ba11a4eecea0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00003","start":147,"end":253,"exact":"Sencer Odabaşi explained to me that “everyone knows they will go outside and that they will get attacked. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b031a759be9867928ae488adaf3958e56f5e1cf984a36448e65278e4e92f81b8","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00003","start":253,"end":342,"exact":"But for them, it is a statement to still go out and not allow violence to be normalized.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2d624f4500d21ce1f2023e8e25276cd762027366cb3a5d4ebd614065328025f1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00004","start":0,"end":63,"exact":"June holds historical significance for pride events in Turkey. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:da03e1de27123a66030ac8e78ab214cb121a709a4bdd9555e8a0134a9b621ed4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00004","start":63,"end":171,"exact":"Once home to the largest pride marches in the Muslim world, Istanbul saw these celebrations banned in 2016. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:bf76167870ad812a39731634788cff21c9d494b6a43db09d3834ca8a29676761","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00004","start":171,"end":300,"exact":"And as Erdoğan secured victory in Turkey's presidential elections for the third consecutive time, the stakes in 2023 are higher. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:51a19997420deb7156d4d4de1ed1e06a1e2d30cf56b1c68afa0c2b1c426161e5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00004","start":300,"end":459,"exact":"Many Turkish citizens are wary of how authoritarian narratives saw a quick uptick since Erdoğan’s reelection, but also seek other venues to exercise democracy."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ed571acff47e33104bbfebe8ca312c088e016cbb11c2a2586037ae618f607c20","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00005","start":0,"end":51,"exact":"The conversations happening in post-election Turkey"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3bb7eb75c91706031600be4ee1a575981a96c54ba580958c8c83e436dd5073da","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00006","start":0,"end":60,"exact":"“Erdoğan is becoming more authoritarian after the elections”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:659d49279e33bf6667ae0012f7ae1767ac0bf879fd926210c90eef2e0ae3fa30","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00007","start":0,"end":96,"exact":"This narrative in a nutshell: “Erdoğan thinks he can do whatever he wants now that he won again”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:93de4506697fc99e7f2363f481b4b17c84e11e2d8d3b1caeddb206d20e578670","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00008","start":0,"end":212,"exact":"A significant portion of Turkish citizens (47.86 percent of the electorate, as indicated by the ballots cast for Kemal Kılıçdaroğlu, Erdoğan's opponent) who wanted a change in leadership was sorely disappointed. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d63e9a38533d9a8b3ce8aa528f0768b8052ccfcac157fc450ab4f654abfb9dc2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00008","start":212,"end":353,"exact":"Their cautiously optimistic atmosphere was shattered after the first round on May 14, and subsequent results only reinforced their concerns. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2b8e1aafaa3ea4c7d92ead72a56e9102686d12d929e1c3106c735f7130f0cc87","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00008","start":353,"end":419,"exact":"Many now find their fears about Erdoğan and his allies validated. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:080f9e9148720c32566c9f942c87324d80a667d2845cd208339ada4d4b28d0d1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00008","start":419,"end":537,"exact":"During his victory speech, Erdoğan targeted LGBTQ+ people and the opposition, instead of his usual more unifying tone."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:445285d98973541f1aefc1d1c2d532e5fb0afe7684aba7955f8e8db474f4fafb","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00009","start":0,"end":179,"exact":"“Erdoğan's terms have traditionally started out relatively softer and progressively became more aggressive, peaking during the election campaigns,” Odabaşi wrote in our database. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:244d1cc0ab8f646889725a5d50523af7e1d7d7f8abf4e872012ce0a4633c94c3","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00009","start":179,"end":268,"exact":"“Directly attacking the opposition from basically day one points towards a new strategy”."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:93aa5094655bf1c020da6b58d6c5168381c16cbe5aae4c2c7d123d131d31dd25","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00010","start":0,"end":107,"exact":"An example of how this narrative spreads online: “Those who wanted to watch the movie Pride were detained!”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f4556060360de26a29d163d2dfebbbf0c70a32ebeba03d2d1d651d75fa3dbb27","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00011","start":0,"end":27,"exact":"Where it is shared: Twitter"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a9d2dc4d7571c58b70a9d49a0805a46541af6b201e6497d525728502bf7b9364","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00012","start":0,"end":70,"exact":"Author: KaosGL, one of Turkey's oldest and biggest LGBTQ+ rights NGOs."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d4c63bd1ca872d6fac62d40d89bd5bac138f1754ee9959480bf37d106f7ce477","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00013","start":0,"end":206,"exact":"Content: KaosGL tweets about a police raid on BEKSAV, an İstanbul based culture and art foundation, after they refused to comply with the governor's ban on publicly screening the 2014 British movie “Pride.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2093ef4dd012d8df26c227067d12cd6afc536e361a09a7a6348b3a12ee511eaa","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00014","start":0,"end":218,"exact":"Context: On June 7, as part of their Pride month calendar, BEKSAV announced their plan to organize a screening of the film “Pride.” However, Governor Muhittin Pamuk, appointed by Ankara, issued a ban on the screening. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:fca1b4b6bd4e8d8ffe34920a0c2c405534b89a7aacb830333d3730be580efcdb","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00014","start":218,"end":332,"exact":"Despite the ban, BEKSAV declared that they would not acknowledge it and invited everyone to attend the screening. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:48cccac2efefcef85a2bad8981937cb9c37d8861d274856d67478669b4516b20","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00014","start":332,"end":435,"exact":"The police forcefully intervened and detained several organizers from BEKSAV, who were later released. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:67e29adc2bb96e5b2f4698a1b00db182f66807a00366ca0e8db1fa0d152cbb92","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00014","start":435,"end":510,"exact":"BEKSAV’s stand inspired other similar groups to also screen films that day."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:760511871ec8759e84ee4fb2eae2b87bc460fd90db3b406cc1e5b2058bd9c62a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00015","start":0,"end":28,"exact":"Subtext: There is no subtext"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5a8f12b193d19e353cac288574e762e015f8ced4ff4ed47da3251cad966f82e5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00016","start":0,"end":63,"exact":"Civic Impact: +3, the highest positive score on our scorecard. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:21d8cff231dd12fbab2601c789662573f61e8104a4f7632363e885e6ad3c42a3","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00016","start":63,"end":200,"exact":"Coverage of the attack on BEKSAV has a positive civic impact because it is important not to normalize authoritarian pressures by the AKP."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2b99cb4e84770cd4a11bdad9afb22f4dec76aa5093ebdb5b57b7baf119e3c6b4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00017","start":0,"end":47,"exact":"See more related items here: 491, 494, 496, 518"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:11fec58db4fc09a1996bb9d7ab745e6520fd8eb7904686adad4739e82237e2f8","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00018","start":0,"end":55,"exact":"See what the pre-electoral mood was with our newsletter"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c79a9a7389b13698a687230ee88c916fb24b98d4291e8e0b1c31c8bfdb5aa138","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00019","start":0,"end":55,"exact":"“What do onions have to do with the Turkish elections?”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:51a260d05e7aef81d50c93946b8c5aeff3995f0a1581ccfe28e9ca37ceccd930","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00020","start":0,"end":73,"exact":"“The opposition should adopt alternative democratic methods to elections”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c7412b748806b736c0c385fcf3becae9fa613a39b0e14a2fbbb06502b6bee65e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00021","start":0,"end":73,"exact":"This narrative in a nutshell: “Voting is not enough; we ne