make people doubt the legitimacy of Turkey's electoral process. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:91d2d20a6a652a97a38c97b6b7b7b7bcc100d3a3a338d81111e8fb24c797e083","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00022","start":339,"end":530,"exact":"Still, the main opposition party, the Republican People's Party (commonly known as CHP), always pointed to the ballot box as the democratic solution and discouraged citizens from protesting. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:77508215f29600d7b3e27a46d005f9124945acfb0ea201c0f9f24af7b4afac64","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00022","start":530,"end":586,"exact":"Many now feel let down by this approach, and by the CHP."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d7dc2b3b87a2d59fe49ee53af74cd0888374b99adee1fdfd2f001e1166fc8a1a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00023","start":0,"end":243,"exact":"As a result, a narrative has emerged urging individuals to participate in NGOs (such as LGBTQ+ groups), informal associations, unions, neighborhood solidarity groups, and political parties instead of relying solely on voting every five years. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ae65414508df288e149427f95192f21cdba47b7c110abb829fe42eefc1579ecf","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00023","start":243,"end":422,"exact":"Some groups, such as the Workers’ Party of Turkey as well as other parties and NGOs, have confirmed to Odabaşi that there has been an uptick in registrations since the elections. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e639d015f991aeded002c1eda89e3ac543df3e6059fb709a4422f1b7714480f7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00023","start":422,"end":477,"exact":"This narrative puts into question what democracy means."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:30f21c5413337e2ac841f9f16a61797a9e71304418a81795834c9ea8a2201c23","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00024","start":0,"end":234,"exact":"“Whether this represents a fundamental change in the Turkish political landscape or if it is just an emotional reaction to the unexpected results that will have a short lifespan, time will tell,” Sencer Odabaşi wrote on the database. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:00e6fc2dd90f7640d690a8a76f50d5f15a939e11deb23947782e03c07b958f95","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00024","start":234,"end":345,"exact":"“The sentiment remains civil and democratic, there are no calls for coups or international pressure/sanctions.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:dc0683e433065d497e4f65ca96d92f16585b42ac9e529cdc910303580ed9a4bc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00025","start":0,"end":79,"exact":"An example of how this narrative spreads online: “We draw the line here, again”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:961a6bab55eb5874bc08978d0b303677fa6b0f678aeee2faf4ed86a8755ed678","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00026","start":0,"end":27,"exact":"Where it is shared: Twitter"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f5fd491a3dc23d3f3a8e1887ea31920282b1e18dc0c532e2419c1bfb336b45cc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00027","start":0,"end":57,"exact":"Author: An anonymous pro-HDP Twitter user, @the_dartagnan"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d3c4196fe865ac7a8cbe37428239a166090066d19bc89a6bf74dc6b7f3a3730b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00028","start":0,"end":274,"exact":"Content: They tweeted a 2016 speech by jailed pro-Kurdish HDP politician Selahattin Demirtaş questioning the legitimacy of elections under Erdoğan and claiming that “democracy is in the streets.” The tweet went viral and the video clip was shared by other accounts as well. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:826af5b563811a055974caef3973f3ccaf4b5b6009e7bf20126d2a6a4bf39ff0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00028","start":274,"end":342,"exact":"The HDP (Peoples’ Democratic Party) is a leftist, pro-Kurdish party."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2f5b9c03873001fd1854b324f3e773b7e63a98991ced14623f8ceb70a0307b90","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00029","start":0,"end":187,"exact":"Context: The speech was made in September 2016 in the parliament, when Erdoğan was calling for a referendum and/or early elections for a presidential system, which he later narrowly won. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6c8512d781fc9a8f26c5c8428c954d8b0e1f3ebe098ef1646d77bd3ee103ebd0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00029","start":187,"end":273,"exact":"Demirtaş was imprisoned that year and remains behind bars without having had a trial. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:942123b474dfa7157dee224273982bcbcb0c9af47a7e8e95e6465c7c96a2a2f7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00029","start":273,"end":334,"exact":"Kılıçdaroğlu pledged to free him, while Erdogan ruled it out."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6a8b76e6c9850917fc2c5588986e9e04fd7432fd7f440a3908212491d31cc28d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00030","start":0,"end":100,"exact":"Subtext: This account claims that Turkish elections under Erdoğan should be considered illegitimate."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c79f40e460b35af401fbe497bb4b4b833c138e133c3ce30e82e498c119e17224","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00031","start":0,"end":208,"exact":"Civic Impact: +2 out of +3, because in an environment where any sign of dissent is criminalized, reminding the people that democratic rights go beyond just voting every five years has a positive civic impact."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:165fce8d69e8e3c0ef0507bcd91723d77dd77aeaa7cf1de5268ecd27ed083dc8","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00032","start":0,"end":42,"exact":"See more related items here: 491, 511, 512"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:82d155b91fe32bf6c8801e06864d768fa801b412a286afafd8cd505058bf7351","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00033","start":0,"end":69,"exact":"“The opposition should only act within the boundaries set by Erdoğan”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:964f11941cd7749bfc5261776d16b6be3b9b22e2a4be38da2b9f7fa0ebe71c68","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00034","start":0,"end":81,"exact":"This narrative in a nutshell: “The opposition should behave like we want them to”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6cae93383d0fcd08345708cafaefd5db2bd156b5c35394e58f7b1e02d6b9d1ba","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00035","start":0,"end":141,"exact":"Erdoğan and his allies have employed strong anti-opposition campaign slogans for a long time, such as labeling the opposition as terrorists. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3942107e824d3af9bfeaeb98ae6f7d8caa53dd73981094a3938efd2cb51a1834","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00035","start":141,"end":220,"exact":"However, far from abating after the elections, this narrative has strengthened."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ca228b9bf7d2a52ae2eaac8ed4485e9d26a83474afb7265d6c3aed6145064891","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00036","start":0,"end":165,"exact":"“The main reason Turkey has not become a completely authoritarian state akin to Russia or Azerbaijan is the existence of an actual opposition,” Sencer Odabaşi says. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:35384b8596904077c558221e97fd134769740928e16809f2c77184115e0384a5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00036","start":165,"end":295,"exact":"“From Erdoğan's point of view, this narrative is about the importance of creating a controlled opposition like the one in Russia. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:17d89b56e10e1c0e17059ea4b74c6efd8a5de2fe66f61041df73e3cdf71fce71","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00036","start":295,"end":462,"exact":"This opposition will be tasked with criticizing the day-to-day affairs of the government while not bringing the fundamental pillars of Erdoğan's regime into question.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f0807eef6a32f3a220513b6f67e815156718c09a3e0baa58d99cf27896a9f680","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00037","start":0,"end":126,"exact":"For Odabaşi, the aim is not to establish a puppet opposition, but rather one that understands the boundaries it cannot cross. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:82b5f16b7a276baf7a8bccb468cf662386b0c67142a6dbb652c2dde9e09f0974","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00037","start":126,"end":260,"exact":"In Turkey's case, this means refraining from criticizing nationalist and religious conservatism, foreign policy, and Erdoğan himself. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3900f48ef12b0bbc2cc328a3d765acfb55455d7a2490420e29a8e251e56a23c6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00037","start":260,"end":351,"exact":"Issues concerning Kurdish and LGBTQ+ rights would also be off-limits within this framework."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d24e0f8a981690c5218684978f857b3d11fa6254c2bff9b0a3253aba56bb6b9b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00038","start":0,"end":104,"exact":"“They could, however, accuse Erdoğan of not being conservative and nationalistic enough,” Odabaşi says. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8761125b520071c3aeaf02b507113741355dd9ba1f19bdca94a7217f68607a8e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00038","start":104,"end":144,"exact":"“Refugee policy can also be criticized.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f8db3a4abb6f0619aa53ba788fffde4481236c611e556e703db4d40fbddf37a4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00039","start":0,"end":60,"exact":"There are violent calls online against the CHP and the HDP. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f971ad06689aa33ff06966a42c7af73cc072c85bb40e1931a25002195df6fe94","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00039","start":60,"end":159,"exact":"Their figureheads may face more harassment through defamation and imprisonment in the near future. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:55fce96d7313ad751991f543da8ce0876fb07212723e4a8b43b1f17b3f3e932a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5","blockId":"gv-790498-b00039","start":159,"end":298,"exact":"For example, far-right party MHP recently called for the prosecution of opposition leader Kılıçdaroğlu because of his “links to terrorism.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:196817b5c49254a93059af04680c9503","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"196817b5c49254a93059af04680c9503","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:6dac3177d1c06ffb85a40e41125eb2c5:u_ab7e480efb4c544a0aff91e5","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:b5b7774ac86fbe7c112ac47939e4c6572d541a127b09252577ae053eb6bd4e04","urn:doxa:passage:91d2d20a6a652a97a38c97b6b7b7b7bcc100d3a3a338d81111e8fb24c797e083","urn:doxa:passage:77508215f29600d7b3e27a46d005f9124945acfb0ea201c0f9f24af7b4afac64","urn:doxa:passage:d7dc2b3b87a2d59fe49ee53af74cd0888374b99adee1fdfd2f001e1166fc8a1a","urn:doxa:passage:ae65414508df288e149427f95192f21cdba47b7c110abb829fe42eefc1579ecf","urn:doxa:passage:e639d015f991aeded002c1eda89e3ac543df3e6059fb709a4422f1b7714480f7","urn:doxa:passage:30f21c5413337e2ac841f9f16a61797a9e71304418a81795834c9ea8a2201c23","urn:doxa:passage:00e6fc2dd90f7640d690a8a76f50d5f15a939e11deb23947782e03c07b958f95","urn:doxa:passage:dc0683e433065d497e4f65ca96d92f16585b42ac9e529cdc910303580ed9a4bc","urn:doxa:passage:961a6bab55eb5874bc08978d0b303677fa6b0f678aeee2faf4ed86a8755ed678","urn:doxa:passage:f5fd491a3dc23d3f3a8e1887ea31920282b1e18dc0c532e2419c1bfb336b45cc","urn:doxa