ian migrants to Europe in return for visa concessions and EUR 6 billion in aid for more than 3.5 million Syrians arriving in Turkey. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:28c85a7934e2b994a2add7335d2b72319e2a68a8222c9a518498f9a953e446f0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00015","start":220,"end":420,"exact":"In July 2020, following threats leveled against the EU that Turkey would no longer block migrants’ passage to Europe, the European Parliament approved an additional EUR 500 million (USD 562 million). "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:efe56383a916fda7dcff039befb4cb0f753d69239d0ada34fe9dae136eb38a38","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00015","start":420,"end":487,"exact":"In 2021, the EU allocated EUR 3 billion to refugees for 2021–2023. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:aa483b63c3b06cb4f08e44410e7bfadf8c9a6d9b12fdaf4ed4fc57e94507e171","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00015","start":487,"end":601,"exact":"Two EU officials who spoke to the Financial Times said additional funds had been budgeted to extend aid to Turkey."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:109b8ee07cadf0d028767dc00e31f5e1f668741b66e743231ec2737213f77105","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00016","start":0,"end":187,"exact":"In addition to Syrian refugees, Turkey has also been on the receiving end of thousands of Afghan migrants who fled the country following the withdrawal of American troops in August 2021. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e9c0742b6cabf94536f11e91813e30cbb818b47096853a4e401f93aff1673328","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00016","start":187,"end":309,"exact":"The United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees estimates that some 4 million refugees, mostly Syrians, live in Turkey. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:349b999d8353a5c3652d2a772ca66e32a444093dcb17fe874ee09a906b09745d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00016","start":309,"end":351,"exact":"Afghans make up the second largest group. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7722ec8255340234a9f045d16757a0ed2a2dfd80ace0ec32dc25d3b1e16787a5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00016","start":351,"end":428,"exact":"The growing number of refugees has sparked anti-immigrant violence in Turkey."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:63c77e2007705df3b06c1d8889da28480165d2c2d37abfc3abe798f792b7dbf0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00017","start":0,"end":132,"exact":"Although additional funds were allocated to Turkey, no progress was made on Turkey's EU accession negotiations or visa concessions. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b5fd4b6ee3b39aab146eaf07cb8ee6ac3f0d556ea14518c6171a0120d008c645","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00017","start":132,"end":268,"exact":"Scores of Turkish citizens have shared their stories of visa denials in recent years, which have extended to journalists and academics. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0f8f343ea8057078f179216814b562321ef3cb89f17437c37b21d65bbf303c1d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00017","start":268,"end":396,"exact":"In July 2023, EFJ issued a statement calling on the EU member states to stop the “de facto visa embargo imposed on journalists.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:82ca2787fd6a569844fb291a10168530e5b10d8902888b98963fa873e0b4fa2c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00018","start":0,"end":162,"exact":"According to data on Schengen Visa Info, out of 768,408 applications made to member states in 2o22, 645,842 applications were rejected in 2021 — about 84 percent."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e989d5189b80b4df695dc4ea2b3b06992da99c7437044be62002f68e424b10c1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00019","start":0,"end":81,"exact":"Pundits say there is a long road ahead if Turkey genuinely wants to join the EU. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0f22f4cea9ad931b0aedaed7ea9a00c0354a35eb16fee0eeaf65077e4a3aaa72","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00019","start":81,"end":213,"exact":"Reforming the rule of law, adhering to democratic principles, and ensuring equal rights are just some of the pressing requirements. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a4be654141d08747564b5832d86f68f623371491d4f52436d694d1e5c34a358e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00019","start":213,"end":423,"exact":"None of these are a problem, according to President Erdoğan, who told reporters on the sidelines of the NATO summit in Vilnius that Turkey had “no shortcomings when it comes to democracy, rights, and freedoms.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9b5a57a8fdcae44feaf7c6bfdab8e33348b19770a7f54207865c2ef7484337e9","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00020","start":0,"end":134,"exact":"As such, it does not look like Turkey will start implementing outstanding decisions and rulings of the European Court of Human Rights."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d3a7c156eaad63069b95edc774a54ca7c87ae2c27255abbcf4640b191c0d0036","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00021","start":0,"end":222,"exact":"One high-profile example of an outstanding judiciary case is that of Osman Kavala, Turkey's renowned philanthropist, who was sentenced to life in prison in April 2022 after his arrest in 2017 in a maximum-security prison. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:61fff857491783b54594a1979e3fc70c6a932d3268a2133c20097bd02e3c2ea5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00021","start":222,"end":381,"exact":"Kavala, a successful Turkish businessman, supported numerous civil society initiatives in Turkey over the years, including the Open Society Foundation Turkey. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:123b1f2cef9ecd05fe1a7f116bfbc2c6f35b1076aa6572d35540557cc0bbc2ae","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00021","start":381,"end":564,"exact":"He was arrested on charges of “attempting to overthrow the constitutional order” and “attempting to overthrow the government” over his alleged financing of the Gezi Protests in 2013. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:31b0730afdcae291b650d7d984c7763bddef2983036525c34aee624495d64492","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00021","start":564,"end":682,"exact":"In February 2020, Kavala was acquitted; however, hours later, he was accused of involvement in the 2016 coup attempt. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:33adbf007b5ced0d6f4100bf2d22531f20969cba70332b4c1cd17efc8630f7d5","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00021","start":682,"end":1079,"exact":"Although he was cleared one month after this accusation, Kavala was kept in remand detention on the charge of “political or military espionage.” Then in January 2021, his acquittal in the Gezi Park trial was reversed, and during the trial held in February 2021, the court ruled to combine charges leveled against Kavala in the Gezi Park trial with the 2016 coup, ruling to continue his detention. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3a0d070567b47a9cc514c1534ac157e0d7ea34dac79a5d0858e808f83e4527f9","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00021","start":1079,"end":1168,"exact":"Kavala's lawyers have said the indictment is a presumptive fiction lacking any evidence. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:80d6ee06f5774c79b100c70b5393954204e284a80660db4c43cc93ede3d22a0e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00021","start":1168,"end":1300,"exact":"International human rights organizations and civil society groups in Turkey have said the arrest of Kavala is politically motivated."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1f4f11fc3df197275a0be0e6fab706fc220d7aa4cb9ba0ba462bdd2f70b445d1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00022","start":0,"end":74,"exact":"The sentiments of required internal changes were also echoed in Brussels. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:25ae4dc20ad046348dbe7076357e34dd624bab158df31ab2968147096bc6ed50","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00022","start":74,"end":203,"exact":"Nacho Sanchez Amor, the European Parliament’s rapporteur on Turkey, said on July 18 no geopolitical bargaining was on the table. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b5dba9ab7680a64fa1b8c1d17c76134b2ba4fcfed551b7d8231e9f2bca1a5f06","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00022","start":203,"end":384,"exact":"“When Turkish authorities show real interest in stopping the continuous backsliding in fundamental freedoms and rule of law,” then accession talks can return, noted the rapporteur. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7e254ff3e6091e2d9b6f58f5cc3409508f4bbc33c9502cf8c2c402f1ebe9d799","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8","blockId":"gv-792968-b00022","start":384,"end":495,"exact":"Other European officials noted Sweden's membership to NATO and Turkey's EU bid were independent of each other. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:e3f74e86c41cd8513e6caf57e9e803d3","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"e3f74e86c41cd8513e6caf57e9e803d3","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:84fdf54b1f618c7772a2da56d62a54d8:u_8e30b7e7a982a63dbc8eb9d6","attribution":"unknown","speaker":"Unknown","speakerStance":"not_applicable","documentStance":"not_applicable","proposition":"","hypothetical":false,"reviewStatus":"unreviewed","unitContext":["urn:doxa:passage:8e41ddacadeed9ff8acb21925a727f3b9a2a7d5275447c67e015f3a8b88cd1e9","urn:doxa:passage:28c85a7934e2b994a2add7335d2b72319e2a68a8222c9a518498f9a953e446f0","urn:doxa:passage:efe56383a916fda7dcff039befb4cb0f753d69239d0ada34fe9dae136eb38a38","urn:doxa:passage:aa483b63c3b06cb4f08e44410e7bfadf8c9a6d9b12fdaf4ed4fc57e94507e171","urn:doxa:passage:109b8ee07cadf0d028767dc00e31f5e1f668741b66e743231ec2737213f77105","urn:doxa:passage:e9c0742b6cabf94536f11e91813e30cbb818b47096853a4e401f93aff1673328","urn:doxa:passage:349b999d8353a5c3652d2a772ca66e32a444093dcb17fe874ee09a906b09745d","urn:doxa:passage:7722ec8255340234a9f045d16757a0ed2a2dfd80ace0ec32dc25d3b1e16787a5","urn:doxa:passage:63c77e2007705df3b06c1d8889da28480165d2c2d37abfc3abe798f792b7dbf0","urn:doxa:passage:b5fd4b6ee3b39aab146eaf07