emke","translator":[],"publishedOn":"2024-06-02","sourceUrl":"https://globalvoices.org/2024/06/02/survey-launches-to-attract-women-journalists-for-training-fellowships-in-burkina-faso-senegal-and-togo/","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/","contentSha256":"a769d6ff8d452f192e921ae064a41a3e97e9da05a2f29ee3b068ae7df4a59595","textSha256":"fc19324e7863413dd4079dfd0e823a76a07a29adf7ca794c2d6f2af1706dd301","archivedRecordSha256":"0821511e0501420b4fd258f3216e26d18446381cdcff0e42177e9da54fd42322","inStudy":"urn:doxa:study:muslim-coverage-1"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359:u_919fec09fbcdd300b8d1f8c0","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_919fec09fbcdd300b8d1f8c0","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:unit:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359:u_db7922a4c10246f39596fa99","@type":["doxa:SourceUnit","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"u_db7922a4c10246f39596fa99","status":"accepted","fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:17dff79485b34732b64322f68a14789d085aeb3192d270473295c31513f9b06d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00009","start":0,"end":169,"exact":"AWJP is a news initiative that was started by Catherine Gicheru in 2020 during the COVID-19 pandemic, with funding from the International Center for Journalists (ICFJ). "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2a54c7a93d4daaa24e30d5edb61aac76f5e9e0bff4652de039bba728910cf5b2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00009","start":169,"end":403,"exact":"At the time, Gicheru was an ICFJ Knight Fellow based in Kenya; AWJP’s goal was to fund a cohort of women journalists in their coverage of COVID-19’s impact on women and children in vulnerable communities in different African nations. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b08921ab9f8f41bf37b5fa2521089e8f5207b0465791799ca64113b3ab0a0c10","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00009","start":403,"end":519,"exact":"Women journalists from Uganda, Ghana, Kenya, Nigeria and Tanzania worked as fellows and received coaching from AWJP."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a99e58ca685c1ce4783e6f9ed9ff014fcd8e597ab32a34fb0742ca44ea6544fe","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00010","start":0,"end":193,"exact":"To return to Sow's broadcast in rural Senegal last year: her story ran on La Laghem FM, and covered breaking the silence around domestic violence and assault in Senegalese traditional culture. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:54895aa0e53a98eae6f6b9694162db6824bf339f33f2d228508165287224377d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00010","start":193,"end":298,"exact":"The term “non-denunciation” or ” failure to report” in Wolof is ndeup neupal (pronounced “n-puh n-puh”). "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ae1c1489066d4b2139e1319bf669e44ed4f005606f744472c6c3c9cf32bc1957","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00010","start":298,"end":485,"exact":"Sow's story was broadcast in both French and Wolof to reach a wider audience, as the term ndeup neupal carries greater cultural significance for local villagers who may not speak French. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:3be90560a36ae58e84b6c9e27a662daa949f3783ce128fee63b0c5868cdefafc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00010","start":485,"end":551,"exact":"She interviewed a young woman who had been assaulted by her uncle."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:cf5a2d48d58d96a598d4fcf5d580d1414644df9d72f5b0610b0f4a57299dad05","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00011","start":0,"end":178,"exact":"Sow included interviews with an “homme culturel,” which is a locally respected patriarch of the community or village, as well as a local Muslim leader (an imam) and a therapist. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:fdc9a4c84391a59f9f48a6828df54c17072fcd6e96ae33231efd577b7a888e21","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00011","start":178,"end":305,"exact":"The imam was quoted as strongly against violence against women, saying the Quran doesn’t support domestic violence or assault. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c2f172c64d627e5dbc6f14c0e6e1e28a62e44073dd688b31ce9509606979f66c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00011","start":305,"end":446,"exact":"Breaking such cultural taboos, Sow said, made her radio broadcast gain resonance with community organizations that support women in her area."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7ca2eaa3d954c436c03e397b8df6fde3ad29d896ddbc67270cc402fe36ca236b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00012","start":0,"end":47,"exact":"“The “hommes culturels” really appreciated it. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:9564f83d979057bb17ed9d349bd48f0b348e364dc141f5542ce2469409bde2d6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00012","start":47,"end":222,"exact":"Because they saw that the production was done in the context of our Senegalese culture … we honored our culture in the broadcast and the “hommes culturels” really liked that. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:41b1ef2f1930686dfaa769421e9ccea0f4b8553acfc806e9e3363ef50263663e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00012","start":222,"end":312,"exact":"We showed that violence isn’t appreciated in our Senegalese culture, nor by our religion. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c9eb95a432ee6ddb2e05471a96816e313a9ae5a39907252f81a8889adc033f7a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00012","start":312,"end":377,"exact":"We had a lot of positive feedback on that publication,” Sow said."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:92ffe78905d863c23dd905f06356e32f548e82ee08f97e005468b657e64b2d50","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00013","start":0,"end":53,"exact":"Sow was happy with the impact of her radio broadcast."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d0dd22b8a2ffa70bcc96cec4869a96b6e3ced92145c59d636dfbf8dd7902fd8c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00014","start":0,"end":216,"exact":"“The women who volunteer for our local community health organization [“Badianou Guokh”] who help women, especially the health of mothers and children … they reached out and gave us very positive feedback,” Sow said. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4a12d738cda6e10f19e4e1d97d79501f8855ed5b080d6036293d6aca97a9da88","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00014","start":216,"end":368,"exact":"After hearing her radio story, Sow said volunteers with Badianou Guokh cited the story in their street outreach with pregnant women and nursing mothers."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b882a2414088d1741c857457289ac286bfeb2232a09f5635fa2e8c56d241fdb4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00015","start":0,"end":109,"exact":"Funding for the current survey for francophone journalists comes from New Venture, a media development fund. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:4a191a5db284287344c11235aa4283fb85a49f68042e6a08b629cde8fc5fcd6e","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00015","start":109,"end":283,"exact":"With the survey results on the barriers facing women journalists in these three francophone countries, Gicheru hopes to land more funding to launch the journalism fellowship."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:224348f969d1141fc68f947d9c8d72232ec833848f97b28be3ae9d36152b450c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00016","start":0,"end":32,"exact":"One question on the survey asks:"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c74f5dae6178c99396023923d823ac3a29ca0cba184b5bbc161982f081767010","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00017","start":0,"end":125,"exact":"> Certaines salles de rédaction ont une politique éditoriale (lignes directrices qui contrôlent et modifient la couverture). "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:98eb9c0018fdb3141ae83198893c7670780a1b55ae3248d736000d478191404b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00017","start":125,"end":275,"exact":"La politique éditoriale de votre salle de réduction énumère-t-elle des lignes directrices pour la représentation des femmes dans les textes ou photos?"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:eefbcd9cbd743a09ce51750e41fcd787093c5bfb82824c8a2c45eb4af7ae7e3b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00018","start":0,"end":102,"exact":"> Some newsrooms have a political editorial line (a guiding policy that controls and edits coverage). "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1a5d9da51669a46cff96b1f1aff35aa7285e5f40e0c0fa7bfaa0ed78f90c1aa3","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00018","start":102,"end":218,"exact":"Does the editorial policy of your newsroom outline any guidelines for the representation of women in text or photos?"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2c21e6c166eb1fd8e5b7fc71767d65e2a8a9fdc82e78ddd9e66d50f0b31e0825","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00019","start":0,"end":178,"exact":"The cultural treatment of women — as newsroom employees, but also their representation in news coverage across Africa — is at the heart of Gicheru’s dreams for her AWJP fellows. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0b58faaf6466a764181ded53448340e28b7b64a09e5e632d769acb0b76be9e75","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00019","start":178,"end":340,"exact":"“Are there common areas between Senegal, Togo and Burkina Faso or are there unique challenges? … The research might tell us there are other issues,” said Gicheru."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ff798032b540aabd0a534a44741d3dac6acdf3676d727591479040f699b684dd","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4145f8be70c9320af514def08b00f359","blockId":"gv-813379-b00020","start":0,"end":126,"exact":"“For Togo and Burkina Faso, any intervention we design will be informed by the research we are conducting now,” Gicheru added."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:5882d407a91badf1e6f8ad499f9b64e5","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"5882d407a91badf1e6f8ad499f9b64e5","outcome":"not_applicable","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e1750fdd782a8456f3","scoredUnit":"urn:doxa:unit:4145f8be70c9320a