wine fermentation since 6000 BCE, are strung on the walls beside black-and-white photos. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:38e6002a410ff50124c7596980b345c5cd55b725092e40fc5397b25087e62fa7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00001","start":347,"end":414,"exact":"Didedas is one of six Georgian restaurants in the Spanish capital. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6af84f89c01d7f76609d087f855f49ed8f8fb930cb78632a877ee986429668ab","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00001","start":414,"end":442,"exact":"Five have opened since 2023."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5fd22f035d918c7e9c46642e6604f707b3ce298705311b8b7a6d00cf50fc5dea","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00002","start":0,"end":418,"exact":"“When we got married, no one knew where Georgia was,” say owners Ana Elbakidze, from Tbilisi, and Alfredo Muñoz, from Madrid; “And when we first opened, almost every customer was trying Georgian food for the first time.” Nearly two years after the first opening, reservations are scarcely available, and expansion plans are on the table, along with expertly prepared nigvziani badrijani (rolled eggplant with walnuts)."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d39e2a52b353afc9ec9d8ec439c70b5e874afa7a978e089fe622407871b0b11b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00003","start":0,"end":53,"exact":"Georgian food is not as unfamiliar as it used to be. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8325bb932af2313c2b619b751f6990a7ffa3b97567b0703bc9f01122601ba7e3","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00003","start":53,"end":178,"exact":"The New Yorker forecast the rise of the cuisine in 2019, and a mass appeal moment has finally arrived across Western Europe. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:2e52c109f5d527871ca881419431414c1c409ba9329f5d93396e01638af3aa08","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00003","start":178,"end":378,"exact":"Outside of Madrid, nearly one-third of Georgian restaurants in London listed on Google have opened in the past two years — far outpacing single-digit growth in the city’s limping restaurant industry. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a9bc00459704d5899bbcf054050a1b8a755dd216f606bfba037af9318ca44220","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00003","start":378,"end":477,"exact":"In early 2025, Denmark welcomed its first Georgian restaurant in the wealthy district of Osterbro. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:53b13fb63e32fdd80a44148f83dd2b9f638e0f2d7f56af3825f1f33bced5f2a0","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00003","start":477,"end":648,"exact":"Michelin inspectors have taken notice, placing the first Georgian establishments in their vaunted guide, with spots in New York City, upstate New York, Madrid, and London."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:5a812a1f42afc98bef25fdca9bd9c1c982476ff4d834e1cd3715e29914e11e61","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00004","start":0,"end":63,"exact":"What is causing the ascendance of this small nation’s cuisine? "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:b23b4a167ed2030ff217fc2d10bf26e3abbe49b394f6e3839e5322b3aad495e2","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00004","start":63,"end":339,"exact":"There are, at first, simple explanations: The Russian embargo against Georgian wine in 2006, affecting over 80 percent of exports at the time, did, in fact, spur a mad dash at specialization and competition tilted towards large export markets in the United States and Europe. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f9a62a0620170c198ac2ac4e91efd380f195353d20dfb2460e495653db203ceb","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00004","start":339,"end":449,"exact":"This came after the successful Rose Revolution in 2003, ushering in a new leader and neoliberal trade reform. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:1e284f23cd9417989411cda694032b6457931e04b4a9508218094eaa8e9e0f37","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00004","start":449,"end":669,"exact":"While the embargo ended in 2013 and Russia is still the destination for more than half of Georgian wine exports, a natural wine trend has been beneficial in boosting both exported units and value to wealthier countries. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:151ddd4f18b90f9b608c61827a626117931f130dc985e1c242e89f7ecd68c4a9","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00004","start":669,"end":815,"exact":"Ana and Alfredo, who met working at a bar in London, moved to Georgia briefly in 2006 before leaving because of instability, winding up in Madrid."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:ce24308cb753894fdb3df57465d3eb852971d449acc993adc93aabb7687bf03c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00005","start":0,"end":67,"exact":"A closer political relationship with Europe may be another reason. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a654167eef05033154dd6d733e6433652a390b3273d4b3abcd24dacd34b2998a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00005","start":67,"end":339,"exact":"After visa liberalization with the European Union’s Schengen Area in 2020, Georgia accounted for a surprising number of asylum applications, enough for the Bundesrat to recognize the country as safe in 2023, making rejections far more likely for most asylum applications. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:0f17eb1945b0f95750bbd842fd615a9c9df9ac3c7ff379903373765dc2c39c7c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00005","start":339,"end":422,"exact":"Legal migration flows, including asylum, remain minuscule in the tens of thousands."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6c8f9e35471f893483a756dd0f7b4073feb84d68efd424d687770d8a089deced","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00006","start":0,"end":112,"exact":"Along with Schengen visa liberalization, tourism in the opposite direction, and from the continent, is booming. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c44fdf74d0ce89c175176780198a250fb8ae8757548c57d845e4762bdee1e897","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00006","start":112,"end":201,"exact":"British Airways announced four weekly direct flights between London and Tbilisi in 2025. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:8ee8526e9996503396326c732ee8238570acc6c47f2b62fba76d7de9dfb5b242","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00006","start":201,"end":425,"exact":"Ana says one of her Spanish customers, a teenager, returned from visiting the country and has learned enough Georgian to keep the conversation between bites of medovik (layered honey cake typical in former Soviet cuisines). "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7693b59795e1a7103e552299c42c50cdb11c508da7220f12437896a72387c08d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00006","start":425,"end":680,"exact":"Such dishes may be attracting ever-increasing tourists from Israel, the largest source of tourism to Georgia aside from its bordering countries, likely from the more than one million Russian-speaking Israeli citizens as a result of post-Soviet migration. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:d2ce540f024e394986df419f025f76f5f589e45dff2a85ee9fa12dade6846291","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00006","start":680,"end":862,"exact":"One might speculate Israelis are keen on tasting Georgia’s more Persianate-influenced cuisine in what center-right economist Tyler Cowen calls “multiculturalism without controversy.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:081a23b1eb97f3073a04487e83637c4fcdfdaf0855202fb335cf44ee748d9c1b","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00007","start":0,"end":127,"exact":"There may be other contributing factors, such as the increasing real cost of dining out, along with increasing costs of labor. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f6ea7ba5a37951be94d819dc9ff7e5684882a7ce6e82e837eb0039d23b006859","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:0530444e03560fdac5763eede07d2fb4","blockId":"gv-829591-b00007","start":127,"end":377,"exact":"These are favorable conditions for dishes made with hard-to-find ingredients and hard-to-learn techniques — why spend 15 pounds on a burger when you could spend 16 pounds on khinkali, a Georgian dumpling originating from Silk Road cultural exchange? "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:4064efce32d1febf417e001f61bcdd82","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"4064efce32d1febf417e001f61bcdd82","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5e433d8a874530","evaluates":"urn:doxa:criterion:anti-muslim-hostility:discrimination_claim:2026-03-operational-1:794fad83018ea1e0de86fe60ff7dec7a18160eddcba979e