5950e6","urn:doxa:passage:be85ae4325b082a23ff49369160e45984ddae7b5a94a390d584e031d54930f48"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e140f308eeb34db1e9e50345bd8a087b3627f415d99a28702712a4be487918db","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00013","start":0,"end":220,"exact":"In this X post, Palestinian political scientist Xavier Abu Eid reacts to the passing of Pope Francis by cataloging the words and actions that made him a friend of Palestine, especially during Israel’s latest war on Gaza."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7c8a05edaa5a3f2cefdf885d9fbe1997591a1f7d38174d888a1ca78719112195","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00014","start":0,"end":236,"exact":"By referring to Pope Francis’s comments on how it couldn’t be peace without justice, the author is implying that the Pope recognized the need to prosecute all those involved in war crimes and the Palestinian right to self-determination."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:eedae34a8dea7d8c8526dfd240429f459310aa548bbbba2306e59c935984f20d","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00015","start":0,"end":218,"exact":"The reactions to Abu Eid’s post, while including criticism from pro-Israel and pro-MAGA accounts, underscore the divisive nature of the conflict and the significance of voices that advocate for a rights-based approach."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:71228a9b9df9548117772b78c9869f0b8e107ccb32764b655d662f7d2aa5c5f4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00016","start":0,"end":122,"exact":"Xavier Abu Eid is a PhD candidate at Trinity College Dublin and a former Palestine Liberation Organization (PLO) advisor. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f6a108c87e62cd5c7138470ee22716c0a85889d1972977465517f1c6a1ca65b7","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00016","start":122,"end":310,"exact":"He was born in Chile to a Palestinian Christian family from Beit Jala and is the author of “Rooted in Palestine: Palestinian Christians and the Struggle for National Liberation 1917-2004.”"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e0c9aa1a8ad877a078bca39a90634f5bb367116013e4a20a6de69bf401d0e580","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00017","start":0,"end":91,"exact":"The item received 25 quote posts, 31 comments, 540 reposts, 1.5k likes, and 103 bookmarks. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:7f42a1792b0732c2479920f008f416072d52907d4de458c2f9c4a61e80de0969","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00017","start":91,"end":318,"exact":"It ranked +1 under our civic impact scores as while mourning Pope Francis, the author recounts the Pope’s efforts for a ceasefire and the need for accountability that the Pope advocated for, replicating the message of the Pope."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:6d3217d356beac824e4b0eff40a6e21c65e1984c34bc66ef88416b636124d8bc","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00018","start":0,"end":34,"exact":"See the item’s full analysis here."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:c284affae9418b5a743896a60d520e14c66e71db9444261884c67f482f5215a6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00019","start":0,"end":238,"exact":"In this X item, Pakistani writer Fatima Bhutto expresses her love for Pope Francis and laments his passing, praising him as a singular public figure who showed empathy and moral courage to support Palestinians and pledged to pray for him."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:18d3d67d2ac81adcde6f7f367e3d70c25690acb40cd2f4bf344421555be08596","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00020","start":0,"end":222,"exact":"Bhutto’s claim that Pope Francis “was the only public figure of conscience and compassion we had” suggests that those in favor of the Palestinian cause are even more alone in their mission now that Pope Francis has passed."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:51b86c11278b27969a25536633103e8c44d789aa1b7a31c3c146a14cb877d483","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00021","start":0,"end":134,"exact":"Fatima Bhutto is an award-winning Pakistani novelist, columnist, and public figure in her own right, with 2.6 million followers on X. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:f913d4f08344dc9736015186b98e3b248ccd9a3ca17319b72264e65c2af2cfd1","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00021","start":134,"end":335,"exact":"She is a scion of Pakistan’s preeminent political dynasty, the Bhuttos, being, among other relations, the niece of one and the granddaughter of another historical politician and former prime minister. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:e9b3114e0cd1926eecfb9ad2590900f000eda9622bc8acff1d213cdf5b9639b6","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00021","start":335,"end":510,"exact":"She has publicly criticized the dynastic politics practiced by her family, is a vocal pro-Palestine advocate and critic of public figures, and is a secularist cultural Muslim."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:68bd60d3edbe492eb765322b7749630fa7ae7e182d8d059f52c9cee8eef79fb4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00022","start":0,"end":90,"exact":"The item received 44 quote posts, 21 comments, 1k reposts, 6.2k likes, and 205 bookmarks. "},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:cc4f9ac3bf3e464d6277f045cb275cfb8686334268c15c7a6154ba9f190fd2c4","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00022","start":90,"end":276,"exact":"It ranked +2 under our civic impact score, given Bhutto’s reach while amplifying Pope Francis’s unique, humane approach to the situation in Gaza and his advocacy for a peaceful solution."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:a177dfcb0b2ab94559ad061e7d896fe5687d313ab4190c426cfa4a3052e06d2a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00023","start":0,"end":34,"exact":"See the item’s full analysis here."},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:76e97a326fc09937ad7744a2b182db8e80753f0ce40aa7b8231e7a0c6e36862c","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00024","start":0,"end":52,"exact":"Read more on the reactions to Pope Francis’s passing"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:bfab37ed9acf14cf1766c5cc53d0277c09ff59942b8cf3d7ee2fb58401947016","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00025","start":0,"end":75,"exact":"Caribbean leaders and citizens recognize Pope Francis’s groundbreaking work"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:passage:89834cf648f27ad551e3ddae2f4f61ad754ceb93bf60d98f2b2972ee26982f1a","@type":["doxa:Passage","prov:Entity"],"fromSource":"urn:doxa:source:4f258bc5614258628ba373af35a79adf","blockId":"gv-833828-b00026","start":0,"end":98,"exact":"Filipinos pay tribute to Pope Francis who once braved a raging storm to meet with disaster victims"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:decision:861675d70c0e63b27f26c74cb5e93f7b","@type":["doxa:Decision","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"861675d70c0e63b27f26c74cb5e93f7b","outcome":"does_not_meet","generatedBy":"urn:doxa:run:b2a2edd4ca7047128a5