5","urn:doxa:passage:782ab5cd0510ccf80153004746ac66e4076fcd2d378cf25e609be5905c02c61e","urn:doxa:passage:714a91e937f6f2470e4caab92afaa58ad17c6a6d7992fc3200b028bd785cb291","urn:doxa:passage:467c87e33e77c64a9ab1f877a38912805552d370a4b082e2cad05bb5b5a86711","urn:doxa:passage:1c4bf40e078fc8fc9de8cc096b299e422d86eaf14250b86ab20ebd6cf3828d0f","urn:doxa:passage:0de3fd43db39795399ccb1f2931cec0fafd817491081e28e33b134f5481e3f67","urn:doxa:passage:4d667c6c85968ddc64b675a49e36ba65d2c25b0e0a2a6050797295bb30b9d69a","urn:doxa:passage:ef84cfe5eca384693d8c1cf41e547952eab362a73aa2deca312a358554e32f25","urn:doxa:passage:01b966782588a40779e5007d5e3983a2e137eb0245393ba53667addbbf13366b","urn:doxa:passage:a04de3b348993ca45de052467440263d682595853cff7f5a966b6ad498f83ffb","urn:doxa:passage:25fe2cd805676900ae4e01963928b757c9606ff34269232e648a43388a16f935","urn:doxa:passage:b3eb4f36077e39c179d978e1e5234ab225e04a493e520358c098b94c68da7e68","urn:doxa:passage:750e77e11e002f7d3166fac426c3a38ee6c90b78036340f1cb2f38d0bb7d828e","urn:doxa:passage:1897611e34d2a3fbee472f7f73de6ce7b26570b0b3c8d5dc619e49d54f48003c","urn:doxa:passage:75343d6cdb42e090a40643c62f9a89a2d4dd9d60dd4c9af5ff1a1c367315a9d2","urn:doxa:passage:6cb605c0f143e1dff4fafea3d6187dc339d4b4f74c5f8f5f1cc6e83a0c6187f6"]},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:muslim-coverage-1:quoted-stereotype","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"quoted-stereotype","title":"Whose stereotype is this?","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"A jewellery advertisement showed an interfaith family. The article attributes the accusation to activists and calls it a conspiracy theory. That wording matters when interpreting the flag.","reviewQuestion":"Check who made the allegation and how the reporter introduced it. Assigning the activists’ claim to the journalist would reverse the reading.","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:784b899f557a471b1b3f82d58d2a4508","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:503354f5f0264b787cfa1bd37e72d0bd693feb10e16070932ad8189f7ae7c778"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:muslim-coverage-1:school-hijab","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"school-hijab","title":"One school decision, two different questions","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"The account identifies a concrete condition for attending class. The next paragraph reports that lower courts backed the principal and that the Supreme Court later affirmed the student’s right to wear the hijab.","reviewQuestion":"A case can support a reading of unequal treatment. Establishing a repeated practice would require records from other cases, dates or schools.","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:7e08d3e3122332f76811e3bd9e9cbefb","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:294dc28cb7dc1c2cc8ebeb8dc8860b61fa637bf0ab80cb2f0bb9bf602e677d94","pairedDecision":"urn:doxa:decision:09f824e6a4af44ac297dc8ec25fc4c85"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:muslim-coverage-1:author-stance","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"author-stance","title":"What does the author actually support?","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"The final paragraph calls for freedom to choose whether to wear a veil. The model marked the author as supporting the proposition about the risk of discrimination.","reviewQuestion":"Read the proposition alongside the stance. Support for a woman’s freedom of choice gives this author-attributed flag a very different meaning from support for discrimination.","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:04abefed865ec931ee95f8a208ea80cd","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:6f23544ef267bad5aa109375ac871a1fa31bf23a4ca264cf67279e99bcb71734"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:muslim-coverage-1:challenge-a-flag","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"challenge-a-flag","title":"A flag to challenge","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"The sentence identifies women as the group barred from care. Neither this sentence nor its paragraph gives Muslim identity as the basis for the restriction. That basis is required by the exclusion criterion.","reviewQuestion":"A reviewer should ask what evidence connects this restriction to religious identity. The published count includes the original flag and keeps this challenge alongside it.","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:46be81204630ae235741744a93c7f72b","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:61df9c18fe16c0cdba5ef9a1bf7801ba52be53d8a2053b7a8caa98e842d671e8"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:muslim-coverage-1:possible-miss","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"possible-miss","title":"A possible miss in an unflagged article","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"The paragraph identifies the Uyghurs as a Muslim Turkic people, then reports labels applied to them in Chinese mainstream media. The model recorded that the group-stereotyping criterion was unmet in this unit.","reviewQuestion":"A reviewer should examine whether these reported labels construct the group as inherently suspect and how ethnic and religious targeting intersect. The article attributes the labels to the media.","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:23f39c04aea7d023d0e5594826b219cd","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:225014e328e3eeeed89363d528626684fa55be5d14f5931646a20912e7a20430"},{"@id":"urn:doxa:note:muslim-coverage-1:biographical-mention","@type":["doxa:EditorialNote","prov:Entity"],"recordId":"biographical-mention","title":"A religious reference can be biographical","authorship":"AI-authored editorial commentary","reading":"The article lists milestones in Samia Suluhu Hassan’s presidency. Her religious identity is part of the biographical description. The cited sentence describes no threat or abuse.","reviewQuestion":"The word Muslim brought this article into the sample. A reader still needs a target and hostile expression to support a targeted-hostility flag.","commentsOn":"urn:doxa:decision:d16abe150d9e8bf60df196c3c0e733db","selectedPassage":"urn:doxa:passage:5495b835a9f350fe8528ce68b927d261b1e3d6a3666c355f631091721db80e27"}]}
